{"id":"synset-1","meaning":"確認","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"confirm","pos":"v.","meaning":"確認（已安排或已知的事）","nuance":"最通用、偏正式；confirm a booking / an order / attendance","example":"Please confirm your attendance by Friday.","exampleZh":"請在週五前確認是否出席。"},{"word":"verify","pos":"v.","meaning":"查證、核實","nuance":"檢查真偽或正確性，常對資料、身分、帳號","example":"We need to verify the figures before the report goes out.","exampleZh":"報告送出前我們得核實這些數字。"},{"word":"make sure","pos":"phr.","meaning":"確保、弄清楚","nuance":"口語；後接 that 子句或 of","example":"Make sure the door is locked before you leave.","exampleZh":"離開前請確定門已鎖好。"},{"word":"ensure","pos":"v.","meaning":"確保（使某事發生）","nuance":"書面；主詞常是制度、措施，不是個人的查看動作","example":"Regular audits ensure that the data stays accurate.","exampleZh":"定期稽核確保資料維持正確。"},{"word":"double-check","pos":"phr.","meaning":"再次檢查","nuance":"口語、強調「再看一遍」避免出錯","example":"Double-check the address before you ship the package.","exampleZh":"寄出包裹前請再檢查一次地址。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Could you ___ that the invoice total is correct?","zh":"你能確認一下發票總額是否正確嗎？","ok":["confirm","verify","make sure","double-check"],"best":"verify","why":"核對數字正確性用 verify 最貼切；ensure 主詞多為制度而非人，口語請求不自然。"},{"tpl":"The new checklist will ___ that nothing is skipped during setup.","zh":"新的檢查表會確保安裝時不漏步驟。","ok":["ensure","make sure"],"best":"ensure","why":"主詞是制度／工具，用 ensure；confirm/verify 需要有人去核對。"},{"tpl":"Please ___ your reservation by phone before departure.","zh":"請在出發前以電話確認您的訂位。","ok":["confirm","verify","double-check"],"best":"confirm","why":"確認已安排的訂位用 confirm；ensure/make sure 不接 reservation 當受詞。"}]},
{"id":"synset-2","meaning":"增加、提高","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"increase","pos":"v.","meaning":"增加（量、數字）","nuance":"最通用，可及物也可不及物；increase by 10%","example":"We plan to increase production by 10 percent next quarter.","exampleZh":"我們計畫下季將產量提高百分之十。"},{"word":"raise","pos":"v.","meaning":"提高（價格、薪資、標準）","nuance":"人為調高；raise prices / wages / awareness","example":"The company will raise prices in January.","exampleZh":"公司將在一月調漲價格。"},{"word":"boost","pos":"v.","meaning":"提振、推升","nuance":"強調帶來明顯推動效果，常用於銷售、士氣","example":"A new ad campaign should boost sales.","exampleZh":"新的廣告活動應能提振銷售。"},{"word":"expand","pos":"v.","meaning":"擴大、擴張","nuance":"規模、範圍、版圖變大；expand into a market","example":"The firm will expand its Taipei office next year.","exampleZh":"公司明年將擴大台北辦公室。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"We plan to ___ production by 10 percent next quarter.","zh":"我們計畫下季將產量提高百分之十。","ok":["increase","boost","raise"],"best":"increase","why":"單純數量增加用 increase；expand 指規模或範圍擴張，不接「by 百分比」。"},{"tpl":"We will ___ prices in January.","zh":"我們將在一月調漲價格。","ok":["raise","increase"],"best":"raise","why":"人為調價最道地是 raise prices；boost 有「提振」的正面意味，不用於漲價。"},{"tpl":"A new ad campaign should ___ sales.","zh":"新的廣告活動應能提振銷售。","ok":["boost","increase"],"best":"boost","why":"boost 強調推動、提振效果；raise sales 不自然。"}]},
{"id":"synset-3","meaning":"減少、降低","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"reduce","pos":"v.","meaning":"減少、降低","nuance":"正式通用；reduce costs / waste / risk","example":"We must reduce costs by the end of the year.","exampleZh":"我們必須在年底前降低成本。"},{"word":"cut","pos":"v.","meaning":"削減、砍","nuance":"口語有力，常指預算、價格、人力；cut jobs","example":"The store will cut prices for the holiday season.","exampleZh":"商店將在假期期間降價。"},{"word":"lower","pos":"v.","meaning":"降低（高度、水準、價格）","nuance":"把數值往下調；lower the price / the risk","example":"The bank may lower interest rates next month.","exampleZh":"銀行下個月可能調降利率。"},{"word":"decrease","pos":"v.","meaning":"減少（量）","nuance":"與 increase 相對，偏數據描述","example":"Exercise can decrease the risk of heart disease.","exampleZh":"運動可降低心臟病風險。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"We must ___ costs by the end of the year.","zh":"我們必須在年底前降低成本。","ok":["reduce","cut","lower","decrease"],"best":"reduce","why":"最中性通用是 reduce；cut 語氣更強、更狠。"},{"tpl":"The store will ___ its prices for the holiday.","zh":"商店將在假期降價。","ok":["lower","cut","reduce"],"best":"lower","why":"降價最常說 lower / cut prices；decrease prices 少見。"},{"tpl":"Healthy habits can ___ the risk of illness.","zh":"健康習慣可降低罹病風險。","ok":["reduce","lower","decrease"],"best":"reduce","why":"reduce the risk 為固定搭配；cut the risk 偏口語誇張。"}]},
{"id":"synset-4","meaning":"延後、改期","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"postpone","pos":"v.","meaning":"延期（改到較晚的時間）","nuance":"正式；postpone a meeting / an event until ...","example":"The board decided to postpone the vote until next month.","exampleZh":"董事會決定將投票延到下個月。"},{"word":"delay","pos":"v.","meaning":"耽擱、延誤","nuance":"可指非自願的延誤，也可指刻意延後；delay a shipment","example":"Heavy snow could delay our flight.","exampleZh":"大雪可能使班機延誤。"},{"word":"put off","pos":"phr.","meaning":"拖延、延後","nuance":"口語片語；常暗示不想做而拖","example":"Don't put off filing your expense report any longer.","exampleZh":"別再拖著不交費用報告了。"},{"word":"reschedule","pos":"v.","meaning":"改期、重新安排時間","nuance":"強調改到新的特定時間；reschedule to Thursday","example":"Could we reschedule the call to Thursday afternoon?","exampleZh":"我們能把通話改到週四下午嗎？"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Let's ___ the meeting until next week.","zh":"我們把會議延到下週吧。","ok":["postpone","delay","put off"],"best":"postpone","why":"刻意延到之後用 postpone；reschedule 要接 to + 新時間，不接 until。"},{"tpl":"Could we ___ the meeting to Thursday?","zh":"我們能把會議改到週四嗎？","ok":["reschedule","postpone"],"best":"reschedule","why":"改到新的具體時間用 reschedule；delay / put off 後接 to 不通順。"},{"tpl":"Please don't ___ filing the report any longer.","zh":"請別再拖著不交報告了。","ok":["put off","delay","postpone"],"best":"put off","why":"暗示因拖延不做用 put off；reschedule 後面不接動名詞。"}]},
{"id":"synset-5","meaning":"取消、中止","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"cancel","pos":"v.","meaning":"取消","nuance":"最通用；cancel a flight / an order / a subscription","example":"The airline had to cancel the flight because of the storm.","exampleZh":"航空公司因暴風雨必須取消航班。"},{"word":"call off","pos":"phr.","meaning":"取消、喊停","nuance":"口語片語；多用於活動、比賽、行動；已安排好的事","example":"They decided to call off the outdoor event due to rain.","exampleZh":"他們因雨決定取消戶外活動。"},{"word":"scrap","pos":"v.","meaning":"廢棄、放棄（計畫）","nuance":"口語；整個計畫被丟掉，含「不要了」的意味","example":"The board decided to scrap the project after costs soared.","exampleZh":"成本暴增後，董事會決定放棄這個專案。"},{"word":"abort","pos":"v.","meaning":"中止（進行中的事）","nuance":"強調半途終止；abort a launch / a mission / a process","example":"Engineers had to abort the test after a sensor failed.","exampleZh":"感測器故障後，工程師只得中止測試。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"The airline had to ___ the flight because of the storm.","zh":"航空公司因暴風雨必須取消航班。","ok":["cancel","call off"],"best":"cancel","why":"訂位、航班、訂單用 cancel；call off 偏活動、比賽，用在航班少見。"},{"tpl":"The board decided to ___ the project after costs soared.","zh":"成本暴增後，董事會決定放棄這個專案。","ok":["scrap","cancel","abort","call off"],"best":"scrap","why":"整個計畫丟棄用 scrap；abort 強調執行到一半喊停。"},{"tpl":"We need to ___ the launch immediately; there is a critical bug.","zh":"我們得立刻中止發布，有重大錯誤。","ok":["abort","call off","cancel"],"best":"abort","why":"進行中、緊急喊停用 abort；scrap 指放棄整個計畫，不是暫停這次動作。"}]},
{"id":"synset-6","meaning":"需要","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"require","pos":"v.","meaning":"要求、必須具備","nuance":"正式；規定、條件、規格；require a permit","example":"This position will require at least five years of experience.","exampleZh":"這個職位需要至少五年經驗。"},{"word":"need","pos":"v.","meaning":"需要","nuance":"最通用；需求可為個人或事物","example":"All visitors will need a security badge.","exampleZh":"所有訪客都需要一張安全識別證。"},{"word":"call for","pos":"phr.","meaning":"需要、要求（情況使然）","nuance":"情況或事態「呼喚」某種行動；call for action","example":"The situation may call for immediate action.","exampleZh":"這個情況可能需要立即行動。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"This position will ___ at least five years of experience.","zh":"這個職位需要至少五年經驗。","ok":["require","need"],"best":"require","why":"職缺條件用 require；call for 的主詞通常是事態而非職位。"},{"tpl":"The situation may ___ immediate action.","zh":"這個情況可能需要立即行動。","ok":["call for","require","need"],"best":"call for","why":"事態「呼喚」行動最自然用 call for；require 語氣較為制度化。"}]},
{"id":"synset-7","meaning":"雇用、聘僱","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"hire","pos":"v.","meaning":"僱用","nuance":"最通用；hire a consultant / new staff","example":"We plan to hire three new sales representatives.","exampleZh":"我們計畫僱用三名新業務代表。"},{"word":"recruit","pos":"v.","meaning":"招募、徵才","nuance":"強調主動尋找、吸引人才；recruit graduates","example":"The firm will recruit graduates directly from universities.","exampleZh":"公司將直接從大學招募應屆畢業生。"},{"word":"employ","pos":"v.","meaning":"僱用（使有工作）","nuance":"正式；常用來描述公司僱用的人數","example":"The factory will employ about 200 workers once it opens.","exampleZh":"工廠開幕後將僱用約兩百名員工。"},{"word":"take on","pos":"phr.","meaning":"接納、增聘","nuance":"口語片語；也可指接下工作或案子","example":"We need to take on more staff for the busy season.","exampleZh":"旺季我們得增聘人手。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"We plan to ___ three new sales representatives.","zh":"我們計畫僱用三名新業務代表。","ok":["hire","recruit","take on","employ"],"best":"hire","why":"一般講僱用某人最常用 hire；recruit 強調徵才過程。"},{"tpl":"The firm will ___ graduates directly from universities.","zh":"公司將直接從大學招募應屆畢業生。","ok":["recruit","hire"],"best":"recruit","why":"從特定來源尋找、吸引人才用 recruit；employ/take on 不強調尋找。"},{"tpl":"The factory will ___ about 200 workers once it opens.","zh":"工廠開幕後將僱用約兩百名員工。","ok":["employ","hire","take on"],"best":"employ","why":"描述雇用規模、持續聘僱用 employ；recruit 重點在招募過程。"}]},
{"id":"synset-8","meaning":"購買、採購","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"purchase","pos":"v.","meaning":"購買（較正式）","nuance":"書面、商業，金額較大；purchase equipment","example":"We will purchase new laptops for the whole team.","exampleZh":"我們將為全團隊採購新筆電。"},{"word":"buy","pos":"v.","meaning":"買","nuance":"最口語通用，任何場合","example":"I'd like to buy two tickets for the evening show.","exampleZh":"我想買兩張晚場的票。"},{"word":"acquire","pos":"v.","meaning":"取得、收購","nuance":"常指併購公司或取得資產、技能","example":"The company intends to acquire a smaller competitor.","exampleZh":"公司打算收購一家較小的競爭對手。"},{"word":"procure","pos":"v.","meaning":"採購（企業對供應商）","nuance":"非常正式；組織的大量採購、供應鏈用語","example":"The department will procure raw materials from approved suppliers.","exampleZh":"該部門將向核准的供應商採購原料。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"We will ___ new laptops for the whole team.","zh":"我們將為全團隊採購新筆電。","ok":["purchase","buy","acquire","procure"],"best":"purchase","why":"公司買設備用 purchase 較正式；buy 口語。"},{"tpl":"The company intends to ___ a smaller competitor.","zh":"公司打算收購一家較小的競爭對手。","ok":["acquire","buy","purchase"],"best":"acquire","why":"併購公司最道地是 acquire；procure 不用於收購公司。"},{"tpl":"The department will ___ raw materials from approved suppliers.","zh":"該部門將向核准的供應商採購原料。","ok":["procure","purchase","buy"],"best":"procure","why":"組織向供應商採購用 procure（採購部的術語）；buy 太口語。"}]},
{"id":"synset-9","meaning":"寄送、遞送","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"send","pos":"v.","meaning":"寄、送出","nuance":"最通用；send an email / a file / a package","example":"Please send the signed contract to me by email.","exampleZh":"請將簽好的合約以電子郵件寄給我。"},{"word":"deliver","pos":"v.","meaning":"遞送、交付","nuance":"貨品或服務送到目的地；deliver on time","example":"We will deliver the furniture to your office on Monday.","exampleZh":"我們週一會把家具送到您的辦公室。"},{"word":"ship","pos":"v.","meaning":"出貨、運送","nuance":"公司將貨品交運；ship an order","example":"We will ship your order within two business days.","exampleZh":"我們將在兩個工作天內出貨。"},{"word":"forward","pos":"v.","meaning":"轉寄、轉交","nuance":"把收到的郵件或文件轉給他人；forward an email","example":"Could you forward this email to the finance team?","exampleZh":"你能把這封郵件轉寄給財務團隊嗎？"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Please ___ the signed contract to me by Friday.","zh":"請在週五前把簽好的合約寄給我。","ok":["send","deliver"],"best":"send","why":"自己的文件寄出用 send；deliver 強調親送／送達；forward 是轉寄別人給你的東西，不合。"},{"tpl":"We will ___ your order within two business days.","zh":"我們將在兩個工作天內出貨。","ok":["ship","send","deliver"],"best":"ship","why":"賣方把貨品交運用 ship；deliver 強調送達目的地。"},{"tpl":"Could you ___ this email to the finance team?","zh":"你能把這封郵件轉寄給財務團隊嗎？","ok":["forward","send"],"best":"forward","why":"轉寄收到的郵件用 forward；deliver/ship 不用於電子郵件。"}]},
{"id":"synset-10","meaning":"討論","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"discuss","pos":"v.","meaning":"討論","nuance":"最通用；直接接受詞，不加 about","example":"Let's discuss the budget at tomorrow's meeting.","exampleZh":"我們明天的會議討論預算吧。"},{"word":"talk over","pos":"phr.","meaning":"商量、談談","nuance":"口語片語；與人商量一個決定","example":"I'd like to talk over the proposal with my team first.","exampleZh":"我想先和團隊商量這項提案。"},{"word":"go over","pos":"phr.","meaning":"逐項過一遍","nuance":"口語；照著清單或文件逐一檢視、講解","example":"Please go over the agenda before the meeting starts.","exampleZh":"會議開始前請先把議程過一遍。"},{"word":"debate","pos":"v.","meaning":"辯論、爭論","nuance":"強調各方意見分歧、公開爭辯","example":"Lawmakers will debate the new tax bill next week.","exampleZh":"議員下週將辯論新稅法案。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Let's ___ the budget at tomorrow's meeting.","zh":"我們明天的會議討論預算吧。","ok":["discuss","go over","talk over","debate"],"best":"discuss","why":"一般「討論」用 discuss；debate 暗示正反爭辯。"},{"tpl":"I'd like to ___ the proposal with my team first.","zh":"我想先和團隊商量這項提案。","ok":["talk over","discuss","go over"],"best":"talk over","why":"與人商量決定用 talk over；debate with my team 語氣變成爭辯。"},{"tpl":"Please ___ the agenda before the meeting starts.","zh":"會議開始前請先把議程過一遍。","ok":["go over","discuss"],"best":"go over","why":"逐項檢視文件用 go over；talk over 是商量，不是檢視。"}]},
{"id":"synset-11","meaning":"建議、提議","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"suggest","pos":"v.","meaning":"建議","nuance":"語氣委婉；suggest + 名詞／動名詞／that 子句","example":"I would suggest that we hold the event in March.","exampleZh":"我建議活動在三月舉行。"},{"word":"recommend","pos":"v.","meaning":"推薦、建議","nuance":"有依據、帶專業判斷；recommend a hotel","example":"Could you recommend a good hotel near the airport?","exampleZh":"你能推薦機場附近的好旅館嗎？"},{"word":"propose","pos":"v.","meaning":"提議、提出","nuance":"正式提出方案、計畫；propose a plan / a merger","example":"We would like to propose a new schedule at Monday's meeting.","exampleZh":"我們想在週一會議提出新的時程。"},{"word":"advise","pos":"v.","meaning":"勸告、建議","nuance":"專業人士給意見；advise sb to do / advise on","example":"The consultant will advise us on tax matters.","exampleZh":"顧問將就稅務事宜給我們建議。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"I would ___ that we hold the event in March.","zh":"我建議活動在三月舉行。","ok":["suggest","recommend","propose"],"best":"suggest","why":"委婉提出想法用 suggest；advise 接 sb to do，不直接接 that 子句較自然。"},{"tpl":"Could you ___ a good hotel near the airport?","zh":"你能推薦機場附近的好旅館嗎？","ok":["recommend","suggest"],"best":"recommend","why":"推薦具體的人事物用 recommend；propose 是提出方案，不是推薦。"},{"tpl":"We would like to ___ a new schedule at Monday's meeting.","zh":"我們想在週一會議提出新的時程。","ok":["propose","suggest","recommend"],"best":"propose","why":"正式提出方案用 propose；advise 不接方案當受詞。"}]},
{"id":"synset-12","meaning":"改善、提升","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"improve","pos":"v.","meaning":"改善","nuance":"最通用；improve quality / service / skills","example":"We aim to improve customer service this year.","exampleZh":"我們今年的目標是改善客戶服務。"},{"word":"enhance","pos":"v.","meaning":"強化、提升","nuance":"讓已不錯的東西更好；enhance reputation / security","example":"The new feature will enhance the user experience.","exampleZh":"新功能將提升使用者體驗。"},{"word":"upgrade","pos":"v.","meaning":"升級","nuance":"換成更好的版本或規格；upgrade software / a seat","example":"We should upgrade our old servers soon.","exampleZh":"我們應該盡快升級舊伺服器。"},{"word":"refine","pos":"v.","meaning":"精進、修飾","nuance":"細部打磨，去蕪存菁；refine a design / a process","example":"The team will refine the design based on feedback.","exampleZh":"團隊將依回饋精修設計。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"We aim to ___ customer service this year.","zh":"我們今年的目標是改善客戶服務。","ok":["improve","enhance"],"best":"improve","why":"改善缺點用 improve；upgrade 是換成更高規格，refine 是細部打磨。"},{"tpl":"We should ___ our old servers soon.","zh":"我們應該盡快升級舊伺服器。","ok":["upgrade","improve"],"best":"upgrade","why":"硬體、軟體換新版用 upgrade；enhance 不接設備整體。"},{"tpl":"The team will ___ the design based on feedback.","zh":"團隊將依回饋精修設計。","ok":["refine","improve","enhance"],"best":"refine","why":"逐步微調打磨用 refine；upgrade 是整個換新。"}]},
{"id":"synset-13","meaning":"修理、修復","stars":4,"members":[{"word":"fix","pos":"v.","meaning":"修好、解決","nuance":"最口語通用；fix a bug / a printer / a problem","example":"Technicians will fix the broken printer today.","exampleZh":"技術人員今天會修好壞掉的印表機。"},{"word":"repair","pos":"v.","meaning":"修理","nuance":"較正式，需要技術的實體修復；repair a machine","example":"Workers need to repair the damaged road as soon as possible.","exampleZh":"工人得盡快修復受損的道路。"},{"word":"mend","pos":"v.","meaning":"縫補、修補","nuance":"小物件如衣物、籬笆、關係；較口語傳統","example":"Can you mend this tear in the jacket?","exampleZh":"你能補好這件夾克的破口嗎？"},{"word":"restore","pos":"v.","meaning":"恢復、修復原狀","nuance":"使回到原來狀態；restore power / service / a building","example":"Crews worked overnight to restore power to the plant.","exampleZh":"工作人員徹夜搶修以恢復工廠供電。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Technicians will ___ the broken printer today.","zh":"技術人員今天會修好壞掉的印表機。","ok":["fix","repair"],"best":"fix","why":"口語最常說 fix；repair 較正式，restore 重點在恢復原狀。"},{"tpl":"Can you ___ this tear in the jacket?","zh":"你能補好這件夾克的破口嗎？","ok":["mend","repair","fix"],"best":"mend","why":"衣物小破損用 mend；restore 用於大型、整體恢復。"}]},
{"id":"synset-14","meaning":"開始","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"begin","pos":"v.","meaning":"開始","nuance":"稍正式；常用於過程、事件；begin to do","example":"The training session will begin at 9 a.m.","exampleZh":"訓練課程將在上午九點開始。"},{"word":"start","pos":"v.","meaning":"開始、啟動","nuance":"最口語通用；也指啟動機器、創業","example":"Construction is scheduled to start next month.","exampleZh":"工程預定下個月開工。"},{"word":"launch","pos":"v.","meaning":"推出、發布","nuance":"產品、服務、活動正式推出；launch a campaign","example":"The company will launch a new product line in spring.","exampleZh":"公司春天將推出新產品線。"},{"word":"commence","pos":"v.","meaning":"開始（公文）","nuance":"極正式，用於合約、法律文件、典禮","example":"Work shall commence upon receipt of the deposit.","exampleZh":"收到訂金後即開始施工。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"The training session will ___ at 9 a.m.","zh":"訓練課程將在上午九點開始。","ok":["begin","start","commence"],"best":"begin","why":"一般場合 begin 或 start 皆可；commence 太正式，launch 用於推出產品。"},{"tpl":"The company will ___ a new product line in spring.","zh":"公司春天將推出新產品線。","ok":["launch","start"],"best":"launch","why":"產品、服務正式推出用 launch；begin/commence 的受詞不是產品。"},{"tpl":"Work shall ___ upon receipt of the deposit.","zh":"收到訂金後即開始施工。","ok":["commence","begin","start"],"best":"commence","why":"合約條款用 commence；launch 不適用於工作開始。"}]},
{"id":"synset-15","meaning":"完成","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"finish","pos":"v.","meaning":"完成、結束","nuance":"最通用；finish a task / a report","example":"Please finish the report before you leave today.","exampleZh":"今天離開前請完成報告。"},{"word":"complete","pos":"v.","meaning":"完成、填寫","nuance":"正式；完整做完或填完表格；complete a form","example":"Please complete the form and return it by Friday.","exampleZh":"請填妥表格並在週五前交回。"},{"word":"wrap up","pos":"phr.","meaning":"收尾、結束","nuance":"口語；結束會議、專案的最後階段","example":"Let's wrap up the meeting; we are out of time.","exampleZh":"我們結束會議吧，時間到了。"},{"word":"finalize","pos":"v.","meaning":"定案、敲定","nuance":"最後確定細節；finalize a contract / a plan","example":"We need to finalize the contract terms today.","exampleZh":"我們今天得敲定合約條款。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Please ___ the form and return it by Friday.","zh":"請填妥表格並在週五前交回。","ok":["complete","finish"],"best":"complete","why":"填表用 complete；finish 也可但較口語，finalize 是敲定內容。"},{"tpl":"Let's ___ the meeting; we are out of time.","zh":"我們結束會議吧，時間到了。","ok":["wrap up","finish"],"best":"wrap up","why":"收尾用 wrap up；complete the meeting 不自然。"},{"tpl":"We need to ___ the contract before the deadline.","zh":"我們得在期限前敲定合約。","ok":["finalize","complete"],"best":"finalize","why":"最後確定細節用 finalize；finish 不暗示「定案」。"}]},
{"id":"synset-16","meaning":"處理","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"handle","pos":"v.","meaning":"處理、應付","nuance":"最通用；handle complaints / a request","example":"Who will handle customer complaints this week?","exampleZh":"這週誰負責處理客訴？"},{"word":"deal with","pos":"phr.","meaning":"應付、處理","nuance":"口語片語；常用於棘手的人或問題","example":"We must deal with the backlog before the audit.","exampleZh":"稽核前我們必須處理積壓的工作。"},{"word":"address","pos":"v.","meaning":"著手處理、正視","nuance":"正式；公開、有條理地面對問題或疑慮","example":"The CEO will address the safety concerns at the town hall.","exampleZh":"執行長將在員工大會上回應安全疑慮。"},{"word":"take care of","pos":"phr.","meaning":"負責、照料","nuance":"口語；把事情接下來辦好","example":"Don't worry, I'll take care of the booking.","exampleZh":"別擔心，訂位我來處理。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Who will ___ customer complaints this week?","zh":"這週誰負責處理客訴？","ok":["handle","deal with","address","take care of"],"best":"handle","why":"處理日常事務用 handle；address 強調正面回應。"},{"tpl":"The CEO will ___ the safety concerns at the town hall.","zh":"執行長將在員工大會上回應安全疑慮。","ok":["address","deal with","handle"],"best":"address","why":"公開正面回應疑慮用 address；take care of 太口語。"},{"tpl":"Don't worry, I'll ___ the booking.","zh":"別擔心，訂位我來處理。","ok":["take care of","handle","deal with"],"best":"take care of","why":"把事情接手辦妥最口語自然；address 不適用。"}]},
{"id":"synset-17","meaning":"通知、告知","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"notify","pos":"v.","meaning":"通知","nuance":"正式；官方、系統、公司通知；notify sb of / about sth","example":"Please notify the customer of the schedule change.","exampleZh":"請通知客戶行程變更。"},{"word":"inform","pos":"v.","meaning":"告知","nuance":"中性正式；inform sb of / that","example":"We will inform you as soon as the shipment arrives.","exampleZh":"貨一到我們就會通知您。"},{"word":"advise","pos":"v.","meaning":"告知、通知（公文）","nuance":"商業書信用語；advise sb of / that","example":"Please advise us of any changes to your address.","exampleZh":"您的地址如有變更，請通知我們。"},{"word":"update","pos":"v.","meaning":"更新近況","nuance":"給對方最新進度；update sb on sth","example":"I will update you on the project status tomorrow.","exampleZh":"我明天會向你更新專案進度。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Please ___ customers about the new return policy.","zh":"請告知客戶新的退貨政策。","ok":["notify","inform","advise"],"best":"inform","why":"告知資訊用 inform 最中性；notify 偏正式通知；update 的對象後接 on。"},{"tpl":"Staff should ___ their manager of any absence in advance.","zh":"員工應事先通知主管任何缺席。","ok":["notify","inform","advise"],"best":"notify","why":"請假通知有官方意味，用 notify of；update 不接 of。"}]},
{"id":"synset-18","meaning":"允許、授權","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"allow","pos":"v.","meaning":"允許","nuance":"最通用；allow sb to do / allow sth","example":"Our policy does not allow employees to work remotely full time.","exampleZh":"我們的政策不允許員工全時遠距工作。"},{"word":"permit","pos":"v.","meaning":"准許","nuance":"較正式、法規；permit sb to do / permit sth","example":"Our rules do not permit visitors to take photos in the lab.","exampleZh":"我們的規定不准訪客在實驗室內拍照。"},{"word":"authorize","pos":"v.","meaning":"授權、核准","nuance":"由有權限者正式批准；authorize a payment","example":"Only a manager can authorize overtime.","exampleZh":"只有經理能核准加班。"},{"word":"let","pos":"v.","meaning":"讓（口語）","nuance":"後接原形動詞，不加 to；let sb do","example":"Please let me use the conference room this afternoon.","exampleZh":"請讓我今天下午使用會議室。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Our policy does not ___ employees to work remotely full time.","zh":"我們的政策不允許員工全時遠距工作。","ok":["allow","permit","authorize"],"best":"allow","why":"一般允許用 allow；let 後面不能接 to do。"},{"tpl":"Only a manager can ___ overtime.","zh":"只有經理能核准加班。","ok":["authorize","allow","permit"],"best":"authorize","why":"有權限者正式批准用 authorize；let 不接名詞受詞。"}]},
{"id":"synset-19","meaning":"禁止","stars":4,"members":[{"word":"prohibit","pos":"v.","meaning":"禁止（法規）","nuance":"最正式；法律、規章；prohibit sb from doing","example":"The contract will prohibit employees from sharing client data.","exampleZh":"合約將禁止員工分享客戶資料。"},{"word":"ban","pos":"v.","meaning":"明令禁止","nuance":"官方、公開的禁令；ban smoking / a product","example":"The new law will ban smoking in all offices.","exampleZh":"新法將禁止所有辦公室吸菸。"},{"word":"forbid","pos":"v.","meaning":"不准、禁止","nuance":"語氣強烈、近乎命令；forbid sb to do","example":"Company rules forbid the use of personal devices in the lab.","exampleZh":"公司規定禁止在實驗室使用個人裝置。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"The new law will ___ smoking in all offices.","zh":"新法將禁止所有辦公室吸菸。","ok":["ban","prohibit","forbid"],"best":"ban","why":"公開明令禁止用 ban；forbid 語氣較個人命令。"},{"tpl":"The contract will ___ employees from sharing client data.","zh":"合約將禁止員工分享客戶資料。","ok":["prohibit","ban"],"best":"prohibit","why":"規章條款用 prohibit from；forbid 後接 to do，不接 from。"}]},
{"id":"synset-20","meaning":"估計、預測","stars":4,"members":[{"word":"estimate","pos":"v.","meaning":"估算","nuance":"根據不完全資料概算數量、成本、時間","example":"Please estimate the cost of the repair before we approve it.","exampleZh":"核准前請先估算維修費用。"},{"word":"project","pos":"v.","meaning":"預估（未來數字）","nuance":"財務報表用語；project sales / growth","example":"The finance team will project sales of five million dollars for next year.","exampleZh":"財務團隊將預估明年銷售額五百萬美元。"},{"word":"forecast","pos":"v.","meaning":"預測","nuance":"氣象、需求、市場趨勢；forecast demand","example":"It is hard to forecast next year's demand.","exampleZh":"很難預測明年的需求。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"It is hard to ___ next year's demand.","zh":"很難預測明年的需求。","ok":["forecast","estimate","project"],"best":"forecast","why":"預測趨勢、需求用 forecast。"},{"tpl":"The finance team will ___ sales of five million dollars for next year.","zh":"財務團隊將預估明年銷售額五百萬美元。","ok":["project","forecast","estimate"],"best":"project","why":"財務報告中的預估數字用 project。"},{"tpl":"Please ___ the cost of the repair before we approve it.","zh":"核准前請先估算維修費用。","ok":["estimate","project"],"best":"estimate","why":"根據資料概算費用用 estimate；forecast 偏預測趨勢，不用於單次費用。"}]},
{"id":"synset-21","meaning":"檢查、審查","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"check","pos":"v.","meaning":"檢查","nuance":"最口語通用；check sth for errors","example":"Please check the report for spelling errors.","exampleZh":"請檢查報告有無拼字錯誤。"},{"word":"examine","pos":"v.","meaning":"詳細檢查","nuance":"仔細查驗；醫療、法律、財務；examine evidence","example":"The committee will examine the proposal and reply by Friday.","exampleZh":"委員會將審查提案並於週五前回覆。"},{"word":"inspect","pos":"v.","meaning":"視察、檢驗","nuance":"官方或品管人員實地查驗；inspect a factory","example":"Quality officials will inspect the factory floor next week.","exampleZh":"品管官員下週將視察工廠生產線。"},{"word":"review","pos":"v.","meaning":"審閱、覆核","nuance":"閱讀後給意見或評估；review a contract","example":"Our lawyer will review the contract before you sign.","exampleZh":"簽約前律師會審閱合約。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Please ___ the report for spelling errors.","zh":"請檢查報告有無拼字錯誤。","ok":["check","review","examine"],"best":"check","why":"簡單核對有無錯誤用 check；inspect 用於實體設施。"},{"tpl":"Quality officials will ___ the factory floor next week.","zh":"品管官員下週將視察工廠生產線。","ok":["inspect","examine"],"best":"inspect","why":"官方實地查驗用 inspect；check/review 太輕，review 不接場所。"},{"tpl":"The committee will ___ the proposal and reply by Friday.","zh":"委員會將審查提案並於週五前回覆。","ok":["review","examine"],"best":"review","why":"閱讀後給意見用 review；inspect 只用於實體查驗。"}]},
{"id":"synset-22","meaning":"合作","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"cooperate","pos":"v.","meaning":"合作、配合","nuance":"共同達成目標，也指配合要求；cooperate with","example":"All staff must cooperate fully with the investigation.","exampleZh":"全體員工必須全力配合調查。"},{"word":"collaborate","pos":"v.","meaning":"協作","nuance":"共同創作、研究；強調共同產出；collaborate on","example":"Our two firms agreed to collaborate on the new product.","exampleZh":"我們兩家公司同意合作開發新產品。"},{"word":"work with","pos":"phr.","meaning":"與…合作","nuance":"口語；最通用，後直接接對象","example":"We hope to work with local suppliers on this project.","exampleZh":"我們希望在這個專案與在地供應商合作。"},{"word":"partner with","pos":"phr.","meaning":"與…結為夥伴","nuance":"正式的策略聯盟；partner with a firm","example":"The startup plans to partner with a major retailer.","exampleZh":"這家新創計畫與大型零售商結盟。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Our two firms agreed to ___ on the new product.","zh":"我們兩家公司同意合作開發新產品。","ok":["cooperate","collaborate"],"best":"collaborate","why":"共同開發產出用 collaborate on；work with/partner with 本身已含 with，且後面要接對象。"},{"tpl":"We hope to ___ local suppliers on this project.","zh":"我們希望在這個專案與在地供應商合作。","ok":["work with","partner with"],"best":"work with","why":"直接接對象時用 work with / partner with；cooperate/collaborate 需加 with。"}]},
{"id":"synset-23","meaning":"達成、實現","stars":4,"members":[{"word":"achieve","pos":"v.","meaning":"達成（努力後）","nuance":"目標、成績；achieve a goal / results","example":"We aim to achieve our sales target by December.","exampleZh":"我們目標在十二月前達成銷售目標。"},{"word":"reach","pos":"v.","meaning":"達到、抵達","nuance":"數字、水準、協議皆可；reach an agreement","example":"Negotiators hope to reach an agreement by Friday.","exampleZh":"談判代表希望週五前達成協議。"},{"word":"attain","pos":"v.","meaning":"獲得、達到（高標）","nuance":"正式；較難的目標、水準；attain a certification","example":"It took years to attain this level of quality.","exampleZh":"花了多年才達到這樣的品質水準。"},{"word":"accomplish","pos":"v.","meaning":"完成、做成","nuance":"強調任務做完；accomplish a mission / a task","example":"The team managed to accomplish all of its goals ahead of schedule.","exampleZh":"團隊提前完成所有目標。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"We aim to ___ our sales target by December.","zh":"我們目標在十二月前達成銷售目標。","ok":["achieve","reach","attain"],"best":"achieve","why":"達成目標最常用 achieve；accomplish 較強調完成任務。"},{"tpl":"It took years to ___ this level of quality.","zh":"花了多年才達到這樣的品質水準。","ok":["achieve","attain","reach"],"best":"attain","why":"難得的高標準用 attain；achieve 更通用。"},{"tpl":"The team managed to ___ all of its goals ahead of schedule.","zh":"團隊提前完成所有目標。","ok":["accomplish","achieve","attain"],"best":"accomplish","why":"強調事情做完做成用 accomplish；reach all of its goals 不自然。"}]},
{"id":"synset-24","meaning":"包含","stars":4,"members":[{"word":"include","pos":"v.","meaning":"包括（列舉其中一部分）","nuance":"最常用；後面可不列完整；included in the price","example":"The package will include a free gift.","exampleZh":"此套裝將附贈一份禮物。"},{"word":"contain","pos":"v.","meaning":"含有（內容物）","nuance":"容器或文件內有；contain ingredients","example":"This capsule does not contain any animal products.","exampleZh":"這個膠囊不含任何動物成分。"},{"word":"consist of","pos":"phr.","meaning":"由…組成","nuance":"說明構成成分；強調全部組成","example":"The committee will consist of five members.","exampleZh":"委員會將由五名成員組成。"},{"word":"comprise","pos":"v.","meaning":"包含、構成","nuance":"正式；整體由部分組成；comprise five parts","example":"The committee will comprise five members.","exampleZh":"委員會將由五名成員組成。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"The package will ___ a free gift.","zh":"此套裝將附贈一份禮物。","ok":["include","contain"],"best":"include","why":"列舉其中一項用 include；consist of / comprise 指全部組成。"},{"tpl":"This capsule does not ___ any animal products.","zh":"這個膠囊不含任何動物成分。","ok":["contain","include"],"best":"contain","why":"成分、內容物用 contain。"},{"tpl":"The committee will ___ five members.","zh":"委員會將由五名成員組成。","ok":["comprise","include","consist of"],"best":"consist of","why":"說明整體組成最道地是 consist of；include 只列出其中一部分。"}]},
{"id":"synset-25","meaning":"選擇","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"choose","pos":"v.","meaning":"選擇","nuance":"最通用；做決定；choose between A and B","example":"Please choose one of the three options below.","exampleZh":"請從下列三個選項中選擇一個。"},{"word":"select","pos":"v.","meaning":"挑選、選出","nuance":"正式；從一群中審慎選出；select a candidate","example":"The committee will select a winner next week.","exampleZh":"委員會下週將選出獲獎者。"},{"word":"pick","pos":"v.","meaning":"挑","nuance":"口語、隨性；pick a date / a color","example":"Let's pick a date for the next meeting.","exampleZh":"我們來挑下次會議的日期吧。"},{"word":"opt for","pos":"phr.","meaning":"選擇採用","nuance":"正式片語；在幾個方案中選定其一；opt for the cheaper plan","example":"Many customers are likely to opt for the cheaper plan.","exampleZh":"許多客戶可能會選擇較便宜的方案。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Please ___ one of the three options below.","zh":"請從下列三個選項中選擇一個。","ok":["choose","select","pick","opt for"],"best":"choose","why":"一般選擇用 choose；pick 較口語。"},{"tpl":"The committee will ___ a winner next week.","zh":"委員會下週將選出獲獎者。","ok":["select","choose","pick"],"best":"select","why":"經審慎評選用 select；opt for 不接「選出某人」。"},{"tpl":"Many customers are likely to ___ the cheaper plan.","zh":"許多客戶可能會選擇較便宜的方案。","ok":["opt for","choose","pick","select"],"best":"opt for","why":"在方案間決定採用哪一個，書面常用 opt for。"}]},
{"id":"synset-26","meaning":"提供","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"provide","pos":"v.","meaning":"提供","nuance":"最通用；provide sth / provide sb with sth","example":"The hotel will provide free breakfast to all guests.","exampleZh":"飯店將為所有房客提供免費早餐。"},{"word":"offer","pos":"v.","meaning":"提供（主動提出）","nuance":"表示願意給，對方可接受或拒絕；offer a discount","example":"We would like to offer you a discount.","exampleZh":"我們想提供您一個折扣。"},{"word":"supply","pos":"v.","meaning":"供應","nuance":"持續供給貨品、資源；supply sb with sth","example":"The firm will supply us with all the necessary parts.","exampleZh":"這家公司將供應我們所需的所有零件。"},{"word":"give","pos":"v.","meaning":"給","nuance":"口語通用；give sb sth","example":"Could you give me a copy of the schedule?","exampleZh":"你能給我一份時程表嗎？"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"The hotel will ___ free breakfast to all guests.","zh":"飯店將為所有房客提供免費早餐。","ok":["provide","offer","give","supply"],"best":"provide","why":"正式提供服務用 provide；offer 強調主動提出。"},{"tpl":"The firm will ___ us with all the necessary parts.","zh":"這家公司將供應我們所需的所有零件。","ok":["supply","provide"],"best":"supply","why":"持續供貨用 supply with；give/offer 不接 with 結構。"},{"tpl":"We would like to ___ you a discount.","zh":"我們想給您一個折扣。","ok":["offer","give"],"best":"offer","why":"主動提出給優惠用 offer；provide 不接雙受詞。"}]},
{"id":"synset-27","meaning":"取得、獲得","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"get","pos":"v.","meaning":"得到","nuance":"最口語通用；get a permit / a reply","example":"I need to get a signature from the director.","exampleZh":"我得取得主任的簽名。"},{"word":"obtain","pos":"v.","meaning":"取得（正式）","nuance":"經過申請或努力取得；obtain a license / approval","example":"You must obtain a permit before construction begins.","exampleZh":"開工前必須取得許可證。"},{"word":"secure","pos":"v.","meaning":"爭取到、確保到手","nuance":"不容易拿到的東西；secure funding / a deal","example":"The startup managed to secure two million dollars in funding.","exampleZh":"這家新創成功取得兩百萬美元資金。"},{"word":"gain","pos":"v.","meaning":"獲得（抽象）","nuance":"經驗、利益、優勢；gain experience / access","example":"Interns can gain valuable experience here.","exampleZh":"實習生在這裡可以獲得寶貴經驗。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"You must ___ a permit before construction begins.","zh":"開工前必須取得許可證。","ok":["obtain","get","secure"],"best":"obtain","why":"申請許可用 obtain；get 較口語。"},{"tpl":"The startup managed to ___ two million dollars in funding.","zh":"這家新創成功取得兩百萬美元資金。","ok":["secure","get","obtain"],"best":"secure","why":"好不容易爭取到資金用 secure；gain funding 不自然。"},{"tpl":"Interns can ___ valuable experience here.","zh":"實習生在這裡可以獲得寶貴經驗。","ok":["gain","get","obtain"],"best":"gain","why":"經驗、技能等抽象收穫用 gain；secure experience 不通。"}]},
{"id":"synset-28","meaning":"參加","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"attend","pos":"v.","meaning":"出席、參加（會議活動）","nuance":"最通用；直接接受詞，不加 to；attend a meeting","example":"All staff are required to attend the safety training.","exampleZh":"全體員工都必須參加安全訓練。"},{"word":"take part in","pos":"phr.","meaning":"參與（活動）","nuance":"口語片語；強調實際投入；take part in a contest","example":"Several companies will take part in the trade fair.","exampleZh":"幾家公司將參加這場商展。"},{"word":"participate in","pos":"phr.","meaning":"參與（正式）","nuance":"正式；強調積極參與討論或活動","example":"Everyone is encouraged to participate in the discussion.","exampleZh":"我們鼓勵每個人參與討論。"},{"word":"join","pos":"v.","meaning":"加入、一同參加","nuance":"加入團隊／組織，或一起參與；join us for lunch","example":"Would you like to join our team for the workshop?","exampleZh":"你想加入我們團隊參加工作坊嗎？"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"All staff are required to ___ the safety training.","zh":"全體員工都必須參加安全訓練。","ok":["attend","take part in","participate in","join"],"best":"attend","why":"出席會議、課程用 attend；join 偏加入一個團體。"},{"tpl":"Several companies will ___ the trade fair.","zh":"幾家公司將參加這場商展。","ok":["attend","take part in","participate in"],"best":"attend","why":"單純出席用 attend；若是展出參展則 take part in 較合。"},{"tpl":"Everyone is encouraged to ___ the discussion actively.","zh":"我們鼓勵每個人積極參與討論。","ok":["participate in","take part in","join"],"best":"participate in","why":"強調積極發言參與用 participate in；attend 只是出席。"}]},
{"id":"synset-29","meaning":"解釋、說明","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"explain","pos":"v.","meaning":"解釋","nuance":"最通用；explain how / why / sth to sb","example":"Could you explain how the system works?","exampleZh":"你能解釋這個系統怎麼運作嗎？"},{"word":"clarify","pos":"v.","meaning":"釐清、澄清","nuance":"把模糊或有疑義的地方說清楚；clarify a point","example":"Please clarify the difference between these two clauses.","exampleZh":"請釐清這兩條條款的差異。"},{"word":"account for","pos":"phr.","meaning":"說明原因、交代","nuance":"解釋為何如此，常用於款項、差異；account for the loss","example":"The manager must account for the missing funds.","exampleZh":"經理必須交代短少的款項。"},{"word":"illustrate","pos":"v.","meaning":"舉例說明","nuance":"用例子或圖表說明；illustrate a point","example":"This chart will illustrate how sales have grown.","exampleZh":"這張圖表將說明銷售如何成長。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Could you ___ how the system works?","zh":"你能解釋這個系統怎麼運作嗎？","ok":["explain","illustrate","clarify"],"best":"explain","why":"一般解釋用 explain；account for 是交代原因或款項去向。"},{"tpl":"Please ___ the difference between these two clauses.","zh":"請釐清這兩條條款的差異。","ok":["clarify","explain"],"best":"clarify","why":"把模糊處說清楚用 clarify。"},{"tpl":"The manager must ___ the missing funds.","zh":"經理必須交代短少的款項。","ok":["account for","explain"],"best":"account for","why":"對款項或差異交代原因去向用 account for。"}]},
{"id":"synset-30","meaning":"強調、突顯","stars":4,"members":[{"word":"emphasize","pos":"v.","meaning":"強調","nuance":"正式通用；emphasize the importance of","example":"The speaker wanted to emphasize the importance of safety.","exampleZh":"講者想強調安全的重要性。"},{"word":"stress","pos":"v.","meaning":"強調、著重","nuance":"口語力道強；stress the need for","example":"The manager will stress the need for teamwork.","exampleZh":"經理會強調團隊合作的必要。"},{"word":"highlight","pos":"v.","meaning":"突顯、標示重點","nuance":"讓重點被注意到；highlight key findings","example":"The report will highlight key findings from the survey.","exampleZh":"報告將突顯調查的重要發現。"},{"word":"underline","pos":"v.","meaning":"強調、加底線","nuance":"比喻用法，強調重點為何重要","example":"The incident will underline the need for better training.","exampleZh":"這起事件突顯了加強訓練的必要。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"The speaker wanted to ___ the importance of safety.","zh":"講者想強調安全的重要性。","ok":["emphasize","stress","highlight","underline"],"best":"emphasize","why":"強調重要性最常用 emphasize；highlight 重點在讓人注意到。"},{"tpl":"The report will ___ key findings from the survey.","zh":"報告將突顯調查的重要發現。","ok":["highlight","emphasize"],"best":"highlight","why":"標示重點發現用 highlight；stress/underline 較不搭 findings。"}]},
{"id":"synset-31","meaning":"重要的","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"important","pos":"adj.","meaning":"重要的","nuance":"最通用，各種情境皆可；important to / for","example":"Customer feedback is important to our product team.","exampleZh":"客戶意見對我們的產品團隊很重要。"},{"word":"crucial","pos":"adj.","meaning":"關鍵的、至關重要的","nuance":"比 important 強，成敗取決於它；crucial to / for","example":"Timely delivery is crucial for winning this contract.","exampleZh":"準時交貨是拿下這份合約的關鍵。"},{"word":"essential","pos":"adj.","meaning":"不可或缺的","nuance":"缺了就不行，強調必備；常見於 essential to / for","example":"A valid passport is essential for international travel.","exampleZh":"出國旅行必須持有有效護照。"},{"word":"vital","pos":"adj.","meaning":"生死攸關的、極重要的","nuance":"語氣最重，帶有維繫生存的意味；vital role / importance","example":"Clean water is vital to the health of the community.","exampleZh":"乾淨的水對社區的健康至關重要。"},{"word":"significant","pos":"adj.","meaning":"顯著的、有重大意義的","nuance":"常指數量或影響夠大、有統計意義，也可指重要；較正式","example":"There was a significant drop in sales after the price increase.","exampleZh":"漲價後銷售額明顯下滑。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"It is ___ that all staff attend the safety briefing.","zh":"所有員工都出席安全說明會是很重要的。","ok":["important","crucial","essential","vital"],"best":"important","why":"一般性的要求用 important 最自然；crucial/vital 語氣更強；significant 指「顯著」，不能表示「必須」。"},{"tpl":"Customer feedback is ___ to the success of the redesign.","zh":"客戶意見對改版成功至關重要。","ok":["important","crucial","essential","vital"],"best":"crucial","why":"強調成敗取決於它用 crucial；significant to 的意思變成「有顯著意義」，語感不同。"},{"tpl":"There has been no ___ change in the schedule.","zh":"行程沒有重大變動。","ok":["significant","important"],"best":"significant","why":"談「變動幅度」用 significant；crucial/vital/essential 不搭 change 這種說法。"}]},
{"id":"synset-32","meaning":"大的／大量的","stars":4,"members":[{"word":"large","pos":"adj.","meaning":"大的、大量的","nuance":"最中性通用，修飾 number / amount / order / company","example":"The retailer placed a large order for winter jackets.","exampleZh":"這家零售商下了一大筆冬季外套訂單。"},{"word":"big","pos":"adj.","meaning":"大的","nuance":"口語、有點隨意；書面報告與數量表達少用 big number of","example":"They announced a big discount for early registration.","exampleZh":"他們宣布提早報名可享大幅折扣。"},{"word":"substantial","pos":"adj.","meaning":"相當大的、實質的","nuance":"強調份量夠、不容忽視；常搭 amount / increase / investment","example":"The project requires a substantial investment from the board.","exampleZh":"這個專案需要董事會相當大額的投資。"},{"word":"considerable","pos":"adj.","meaning":"可觀的、相當多的","nuance":"正式；強調程度或數量值得注意；considerable effort / time","example":"Setting up the new plant took considerable time.","exampleZh":"新廠房的設置花了相當長的時間。"},{"word":"sizable","pos":"adj.","meaning":"相當大的","nuance":"指尺寸或規模頗大，略正式；sizable profit / crowd","example":"A sizable crowd gathered outside the exhibition hall.","exampleZh":"展覽館外聚集了一大群人。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"The company placed a ___ order with our supplier.","zh":"這家公司向我們的供應商下了一筆大訂單。","ok":["large","big","substantial","considerable","sizable"],"best":"large","why":"訂單量大用 large 最中性；substantial/considerable 更書面。"},{"tpl":"We saved a ___ amount of money by switching vendors.","zh":"換供應商讓我們省下一大筆錢。","ok":["large","substantial","considerable","sizable"],"best":"considerable","why":"amount 搭 considerable/substantial 最道地；big amount 口語、不夠書面。"},{"tpl":"A ___ number of applicants had no relevant experience.","zh":"相當多的應徵者沒有相關經驗。","ok":["large","considerable","substantial","sizable"],"best":"large","why":"a large number of 是固定高頻搭配；big number 較口語。"}]},
{"id":"synset-33","meaning":"小的／少量的","stars":4,"members":[{"word":"small","pos":"adj.","meaning":"小的、少量的","nuance":"最通用，指尺寸或數量","example":"Only a small change is needed in the contract wording.","exampleZh":"合約措辭只需要一個小改動。"},{"word":"minor","pos":"adj.","meaning":"次要的、輕微的","nuance":"與 major 相對，強調重要性低；minor repair / issue","example":"The printer has a minor fault that is easy to fix.","exampleZh":"印表機有個容易修好的小故障。"},{"word":"slight","pos":"adj.","meaning":"輕微的、些微的","nuance":"程度很小、幾乎不明顯；slight delay / increase","example":"There was a slight delay in the delivery.","exampleZh":"出貨有輕微延誤。"},{"word":"modest","pos":"adj.","meaning":"適度的、不大的","nuance":"數字不大但可接受，常搭 increase / budget / profit","example":"The firm reported a modest profit this quarter.","exampleZh":"公司本季獲利不算大。"},{"word":"minimal","pos":"adj.","meaning":"最小的、微乎其微的","nuance":"小到近乎沒有；minimal risk / cost / impact","example":"The new process requires minimal training.","exampleZh":"新流程只需要極少的訓練。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Only a ___ change is needed in the contract wording.","zh":"合約措辭只需要一個小改動。","ok":["small","minor","slight","modest","minimal"],"best":"minor","why":"改動「不重要」用 minor 最貼切；slight 偏程度，modest 偏規模。"},{"tpl":"The delay caused only ___ inconvenience to passengers.","zh":"延誤只對乘客造成輕微不便。","ok":["minor","slight","minimal"],"best":"slight","why":"inconvenience 為不可數名詞，搭 slight/minor/minimal；modest inconvenience 不自然。"},{"tpl":"We expect a ___ increase in sales next quarter.","zh":"我們預期下季銷售小幅成長。","ok":["small","slight","modest"],"best":"modest","why":"預測中「不誇張的成長」常用 modest increase；minor/minimal increase 不常見。"}]},
{"id":"synset-34","meaning":"便宜的","stars":4,"members":[{"word":"cheap","pos":"adj.","meaning":"便宜的（有時帶低品質意味）","nuance":"口語最常用；形容價格低，有時暗示廉價貨","example":"This printer is cheap, so we bought ten of them.","exampleZh":"這台印表機很便宜，所以我們買了十台。"},{"word":"inexpensive","pos":"adj.","meaning":"不貴的","nuance":"中性、褒意，強調價格不高但不是劣質","example":"The cafeteria serves inexpensive meals to employees.","exampleZh":"員工餐廳提供價格不貴的餐點。"},{"word":"affordable","pos":"adj.","meaning":"負擔得起的","nuance":"強調一般人付得起，常用於房價、保險、行銷文案","example":"The company aims to offer affordable housing for workers.","exampleZh":"公司希望為員工提供負擔得起的住房。"},{"word":"reasonable","pos":"adj.","meaning":"價格合理的","nuance":"價格公道、物有所值；reasonable price / rate","example":"The hotel offers rooms at a reasonable price.","exampleZh":"這間旅館的房價相當合理。"},{"word":"economical","pos":"adj.","meaning":"經濟實惠的、省錢的","nuance":"強調使用起來省成本，常指車、設備、方案","example":"A hybrid van is the most economical choice for deliveries.","exampleZh":"油電混合貨車是送貨最划算的選擇。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"We are looking for ___ ways to ship small parcels.","zh":"我們在找運送小包裹的省錢方法。","ok":["cheap","affordable","inexpensive","economical"],"best":"affordable","why":"複數名詞前可直接代入；reasonable ways 不通順。"},{"tpl":"The hotel offers rooms at very ___ prices.","zh":"這間旅館的房價很合理。","ok":["reasonable","affordable"],"best":"reasonable","why":"prices 搭 reasonable/affordable；inexpensive prices 不自然，cheap prices 偏口語貶意。"},{"tpl":"This printer is ___, so we bought ten of them.","zh":"這台印表機很便宜，所以我們買了十台。","ok":["cheap","inexpensive","affordable"],"best":"inexpensive","why":"表示價格低又不貶低品質用 inexpensive；cheap 可能暗示品質差。"}]},
{"id":"synset-35","meaning":"昂貴的","stars":4,"members":[{"word":"expensive","pos":"adj.","meaning":"昂貴的","nuance":"最通用，單純指價格高","example":"The restaurant is nice but a little expensive for lunch.","exampleZh":"這家餐廳不錯，但午餐有點貴。"},{"word":"costly","pos":"adj.","meaning":"代價高昂的","nuance":"比 expensive 書面，常指花費大或後果代價大；costly mistake","example":"A single error could prove costly for the firm.","exampleZh":"單一失誤就可能讓公司付出高昂代價。"},{"word":"pricey","pos":"adj.","meaning":"價位偏高的（口語）","nuance":"口語、略帶抱怨","example":"The new laptop is a bit pricey for our budget.","exampleZh":"這台新筆電對我們的預算來說有點貴。"},{"word":"exorbitant","pos":"adj.","meaning":"（價格）過高離譜的","nuance":"貶義，指索價不合理；exorbitant fees / prices","example":"They refused to pay the exorbitant fees the broker demanded.","exampleZh":"他們拒絕支付仲介索取的離譜費用。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Replacing the whole system would be too ___.","zh":"換掉整套系統太貴了。","ok":["expensive","costly","pricey"],"best":"expensive","why":"too 後接一般貴用 expensive；exorbitant 本身已是過度，不搭 too。"},{"tpl":"A single mistake could prove ___ for the firm.","zh":"單一失誤就可能讓公司付出慘痛代價。","ok":["costly","expensive"],"best":"costly","why":"「付出代價」的比喻用 costly 最道地；pricey 太口語。"},{"tpl":"The cafe is lovely, but a little ___ for a quick lunch.","zh":"這間咖啡廳很棒，但拿來吃簡單午餐有點貴。","ok":["expensive","pricey"],"best":"pricey","why":"口語閒聊抱怨價位用 pricey；costly 偏書面、後果導向。"}]},
{"id":"synset-36","meaning":"快速的","stars":4,"members":[{"word":"quick","pos":"adj.","meaning":"快的、迅速的","nuance":"最通用，指動作短、花時間少；a quick look / reply","example":"Let me take a quick look at the budget.","exampleZh":"讓我快速看一下預算。"},{"word":"rapid","pos":"adj.","meaning":"快速的（變化、成長）","nuance":"正式，常搭 growth / change / expansion","example":"The firm has seen rapid growth in Asian markets.","exampleZh":"該公司在亞洲市場快速成長。"},{"word":"prompt","pos":"adj.","meaning":"迅速的、及時的","nuance":"指不拖延、準時回應；prompt reply / payment / service","example":"Thank you for your prompt reply.","exampleZh":"謝謝您迅速的回覆。"},{"word":"swift","pos":"adj.","meaning":"迅捷的","nuance":"書面、帶褒意，常搭 action / response / recovery","example":"The manager took swift action to fix the problem.","exampleZh":"經理迅速採取行動解決了問題。"},{"word":"speedy","pos":"adj.","meaning":"快速的","nuance":"口語、廣告式，常搭 delivery / recovery","example":"We guarantee speedy delivery on all orders.","exampleZh":"我們保證所有訂單快速出貨。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Thank you for your ___ reply.","zh":"謝謝您迅速的回覆。","ok":["quick","prompt","swift","speedy","rapid"],"best":"prompt","why":"商務書信感謝對方「沒有拖延」用 prompt 最道地。"},{"tpl":"The company has seen ___ growth in Asian markets.","zh":"公司在亞洲市場快速成長。","ok":["rapid","swift"],"best":"rapid","why":"growth/expansion 搭 rapid；quick growth、speedy growth 不自然。"},{"tpl":"We need a ___ solution to the parts shortage.","zh":"我們需要盡快解決零件短缺。","ok":["quick","rapid","swift","speedy","prompt"],"best":"quick","why":"一般「速成」的解法用 quick；prompt 強調不拖延，rapid 偏變化速度。"}]},
{"id":"synset-37","meaning":"很多的","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"many","pos":"det.","meaning":"許多（可數）","nuance":"最通用；否定、疑問句最自然，肯定句書面也可用","example":"The report lists many examples of good practice.","exampleZh":"報告列出許多良好實務的例子。"},{"word":"numerous","pos":"adj.","meaning":"為數眾多的","nuance":"書面、正式；強調數量龐大","example":"We have received numerous complaints about the new policy.","exampleZh":"我們收到許多對新政策的抱怨。"},{"word":"a number of","pos":"phr.","meaning":"若干、不少","nuance":"搭複數可數名詞，動詞用複數；the number of 則是單數","example":"A number of employees requested flexible hours.","exampleZh":"有不少員工要求彈性工時。"},{"word":"plenty of","pos":"phr.","meaning":"充足的、很多的","nuance":"口語，可接可數與不可數，帶「夠用」意味","example":"There is plenty of parking behind the office.","exampleZh":"辦公室後方有很多停車位。"},{"word":"countless","pos":"adj.","meaning":"無數的","nuance":"誇張語氣，多到數不清","example":"The product has won countless awards over the years.","exampleZh":"這項產品多年來贏得無數獎項。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"We have received ___ complaints about the new policy.","zh":"我們收到許多對新政策的抱怨。","ok":["many","numerous","a number of","plenty of","countless"],"best":"numerous","why":"書面報告用 numerous 最自然；plenty of 口語，countless 誇飾。"},{"tpl":"Are there ___ vacancies in the sales department?","zh":"業務部有很多職缺嗎？","ok":["many","numerous","plenty of"],"best":"many","why":"疑問句用 many 最自然；a number of 與 countless 在疑問句中不自然。"},{"tpl":"The brochure highlights ___ reasons to choose our service.","zh":"手冊強調選擇我們服務的許多理由。","ok":["numerous","many","a number of","countless"],"best":"numerous","why":"行銷文案用 numerous 或 many；plenty of reasons 偏口語。"}]},
{"id":"synset-38","meaning":"利潤／收益","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"profit","pos":"n.","meaning":"利潤、獲利","nuance":"收入減去成本後的盈餘；net profit / make a profit","example":"The firm made a profit of two million dollars last year.","exampleZh":"公司去年賺了兩百萬美元的利潤。"},{"word":"earnings","pos":"n.","meaning":"收益、盈餘（常用複數）","nuance":"公司財報或個人所得，earnings report / per share","example":"Quarterly earnings rose 12 percent after the product launch.","exampleZh":"產品上市後，季度盈餘成長了百分之十二。"},{"word":"gain","pos":"n.","meaning":"獲利、增加","nuance":"泛指增加或價差獲利，capital gain / productivity gain","example":"The fund reported a six percent gain last year.","exampleZh":"這檔基金去年有百分之六的獲利。"},{"word":"return","pos":"n.","meaning":"投資報酬","nuance":"投入資金換得的回報；return on investment (ROI)","example":"Investors expect a good return on their money.","exampleZh":"投資人期待資金有良好的報酬。"},{"word":"margin","pos":"n.","meaning":"利潤率、毛利","nuance":"營收與成本的差距，常以百分比表示；profit margin","example":"Higher raw material costs cut into our margin.","exampleZh":"原料成本上升壓縮了我們的毛利。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Higher raw material costs cut into our ___.","zh":"原料成本上升侵蝕了我們的利潤。","ok":["profit","earnings","margin"],"best":"margin","why":"成本壓縮的是「利潤率」，margin 最貼切；profit 也行但較籠統。"},{"tpl":"The fund delivered a six percent ___ last year.","zh":"這檔基金去年有百分之六的報酬。","ok":["return","gain","profit"],"best":"return","why":"投資績效以 return 為標準說法；gain 是增值，profit 是絕對金額。"},{"tpl":"Quarterly ___ rose sharply after the product launch.","zh":"產品上市後季度獲利大幅成長。","ok":["earnings","profit","margin"],"best":"earnings","why":"季報用語偏 earnings；margin 指比率。"}]},
{"id":"synset-39","meaning":"費用","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"cost","pos":"n.","meaning":"成本、費用","nuance":"最廣，指為取得某物所需付出的金額；cost of living / labor cost","example":"Please reimburse the full cost of my hotel stay.","exampleZh":"請核銷我住宿的全部費用。"},{"word":"expense","pos":"n.","meaning":"開銷、支出","nuance":"公司帳上花掉的錢；expense report / travel expenses","example":"Meals are treated as a business expense.","exampleZh":"餐費被視為業務開銷。"},{"word":"fee","pos":"n.","meaning":"服務費、規費","nuance":"付給專業人士或機構的固定費用；registration fee / membership fee","example":"The university charges a one-time registration fee.","exampleZh":"這所大學收取一次性的註冊費。"},{"word":"charge","pos":"n.","meaning":"收費、索價","nuance":"服務或商品的收費項目；extra charge / no charge","example":"There is no extra charge for early check-in.","exampleZh":"提早入住不另外收費。"},{"word":"expenditure","pos":"n.","meaning":"經費支出（總額）","nuance":"正式、會計或政府用語，指總支出；public expenditure","example":"The government plans to reduce military expenditure.","exampleZh":"政府計畫縮減軍事支出。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"There is no extra ___ for early check-in.","zh":"提早入住不另外收費。","ok":["charge","fee","cost","expense"],"best":"charge","why":"「額外收費項目」用 charge；fee 偏固定名目，cost 偏成本。"},{"tpl":"Please itemize each ___ on the claim form.","zh":"請在核銷單上逐項列出每筆費用。","ok":["expense","charge","cost","fee"],"best":"expense","why":"報帳情境逐筆列支出用 expense；charge 偏收費項目，fee 偏名目費。"},{"tpl":"The university charges a one-time registration ___.","zh":"這所大學收取一次性的註冊費。","ok":["fee","charge"],"best":"fee","why":"registration fee 是固定搭配；cost 與 expense 不這樣用。"}]},
{"id":"synset-40","meaning":"工作／職位","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"job","pos":"n.","meaning":"工作、職缺","nuance":"最口語通用；find a job / job opening","example":"She found a job at a logistics company.","exampleZh":"她在一家物流公司找到了工作。"},{"word":"position","pos":"n.","meaning":"職位、職缺","nuance":"正式，強調職務與層級；apply for a position / fill a position","example":"The company plans to fill the vacant position by June.","exampleZh":"公司計畫六月前補足這個職缺。"},{"word":"post","pos":"n.","meaning":"職位（常為公職、正式任命）","nuance":"書面、較正式，常指被任命的職務；take up a post","example":"He was appointed to a senior post at the head office.","exampleZh":"他被任命擔任總公司的資深職務。"},{"word":"role","pos":"n.","meaning":"角色、職責","nuance":"強調在團隊或專案中的功能；play a role / leadership role","example":"She took on a leadership role during the merger.","exampleZh":"她在合併期間擔任領導角色。"},{"word":"occupation","pos":"n.","meaning":"職業","nuance":"表格與統計用語，指行業類別而非單一職缺","example":"Please write your occupation in the box at the bottom of the form.","exampleZh":"請在表格底部的方框內填寫您的職業。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"She applied for a ___ in the marketing department.","zh":"她申請了行銷部的一個職位。","ok":["job","position","post","role"],"best":"position","why":"申請職缺的正式用字是 position；job 口語，occupation 不指職缺。"},{"tpl":"He took on a leadership ___ during the merger.","zh":"他在合併期間擔任領導角色。","ok":["role","position"],"best":"role","why":"leadership role 是慣用搭配，強調職責；position 偏頭銜。"},{"tpl":"The company plans to fill the vacant ___ by June.","zh":"公司計畫六月前補足這個空缺。","ok":["position","post","job"],"best":"position","why":"vacant position 最常見；post 較正式或公職。"}]},
{"id":"synset-41","meaning":"會議","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"meeting","pos":"n.","meaning":"會議","nuance":"最通用，不分規模；hold / attend a meeting","example":"Everyone must attend the meeting on Monday morning.","exampleZh":"週一早上大家都必須出席會議。"},{"word":"conference","pos":"n.","meaning":"大型會議、研討會","nuance":"規模大、常跨公司或跨國，通常有議程與演講；annual conference","example":"She gave a presentation at an international conference in Berlin.","exampleZh":"她在柏林的國際研討會上做了簡報。"},{"word":"session","pos":"n.","meaning":"（一場）會期、場次","nuance":"會議或培訓中的一個時段；training session / morning session","example":"The afternoon session will focus on safety rules.","exampleZh":"下午的場次將聚焦於安全規定。"},{"word":"briefing","pos":"n.","meaning":"簡報會、情況說明會","nuance":"資訊由上而下告知，不求討論；press briefing","example":"The manager held a short briefing to explain the new rules.","exampleZh":"經理召開簡短說明會解釋新規定。"},{"word":"seminar","pos":"n.","meaning":"研討會、講習","nuance":"偏教育訓練，有講者與學員；hold a seminar","example":"The seminar on data security attracted over 100 participants.","exampleZh":"資料安全研討會吸引了一百多人參加。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Everyone must attend the ___ on Monday morning.","zh":"週一早上大家都必須出席。","ok":["meeting","briefing","session","conference","seminar"],"best":"meeting","why":"一般內部會議用 meeting；其他成員有特定形式。"},{"tpl":"She gave a presentation at an international ___ in Berlin.","zh":"她在柏林的國際研討會上做了簡報。","ok":["conference","seminar","meeting"],"best":"conference","why":"國際、大型、有多場講者用 conference；briefing 不是這種場合。"},{"tpl":"The manager held a short ___ to explain the new safety rules.","zh":"經理召開簡短說明會解釋新安全規定。","ok":["briefing","meeting","session"],"best":"briefing","why":"單向告知資訊用 briefing；seminar 偏講習，conference 規模太大。"}]},
{"id":"synset-42","meaning":"員工","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"employee","pos":"n.","meaning":"員工（個人）","nuance":"與 employer 相對，指受僱者個體；full-time employee","example":"Each employee is entitled to ten days of paid leave.","exampleZh":"每位員工享有十天帶薪假。"},{"word":"staff","pos":"n.","meaning":"全體職員（集合名詞）","nuance":"視為整體，不加 s；a staff member / sales staff","example":"All staff must wear ID badges inside the building.","exampleZh":"全體職員在大樓內必須配戴識別證。"},{"word":"personnel","pos":"n.","meaning":"人員、人事","nuance":"正式，集合名詞；personnel department / military personnel","example":"Only authorized personnel may enter the control room.","exampleZh":"僅限獲授權人員進入控制室。"},{"word":"workforce","pos":"n.","meaning":"勞動力、全體員工","nuance":"指公司或地區的整體勞動人口；expand the workforce","example":"The company plans to expand its workforce by 20 percent.","exampleZh":"公司計畫將員工規模擴大百分之二十。"},{"word":"worker","pos":"n.","meaning":"工人、勞工","nuance":"強調做事的人，常指基層或勞力工作；factory worker","example":"Each worker must complete the safety course.","exampleZh":"每位工人都必須完成安全課程。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"All ___ must wear ID badges inside the building.","zh":"所有人員在大樓內必須配戴識別證。","ok":["staff","personnel"],"best":"staff","why":"All staff 是集合用法；employee、worker 為單數不能直接接 All。"},{"tpl":"Each ___ is entitled to ten days of paid leave.","zh":"每位員工享有十天帶薪假。","ok":["employee","worker"],"best":"employee","why":"休假等福利權益以 employee 指稱；staff、personnel 是集合名詞，不能加 Each。"},{"tpl":"The company plans to expand its ___ by 20 percent next year.","zh":"公司計畫明年將人力擴編百分之二十。","ok":["workforce","staff","personnel"],"best":"workforce","why":"指整體勞動力規模用 workforce。"}]},
{"id":"synset-43","meaning":"顧客","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"customer","pos":"n.","meaning":"顧客","nuance":"最通用，買商品或服務的人；customer service","example":"The store offers a discount to every customer who spends over $100.","exampleZh":"消費滿一百美元的每位顧客都有折扣。"},{"word":"client","pos":"n.","meaning":"客戶、委託人","nuance":"與專業服務（律師、顧問、廣告）有長期關係；client meeting","example":"The law firm sent a draft contract to its new client.","exampleZh":"律師事務所把合約草稿寄給新客戶。"},{"word":"consumer","pos":"n.","meaning":"消費者","nuance":"指整體市場中的使用者，常用於統計與政策；consumer confidence","example":"Rising consumer confidence boosted retail sales.","exampleZh":"消費者信心回升帶動零售銷售。"},{"word":"patron","pos":"n.","meaning":"（店家的）常客、贊助者","nuance":"正式或優雅，餐廳、劇院、圖書館用；regular patron","example":"Parking is reserved for patron use only.","exampleZh":"停車位僅供光顧的顧客使用。"},{"word":"shopper","pos":"n.","meaning":"購物者","nuance":"指正在逛街或網購的人；online shopper","example":"Every shopper receives a coupon at the entrance.","exampleZh":"每位購物者在入口都會拿到優惠券。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"The store offers a discount to every ___ who spends over $100.","zh":"消費滿一百美元的每位顧客都有折扣。","ok":["customer","shopper","patron"],"best":"customer","why":"最通用的買方稱呼；consumer 指市場整體，不用於 every 這種個別情境。"},{"tpl":"The law firm sent a draft contract to its new ___.","zh":"律師事務所把合約草稿寄給新客戶。","ok":["client","customer"],"best":"client","why":"專業服務的對象用 client。"},{"tpl":"Rising ___ confidence boosted retail sales.","zh":"消費者信心回升帶動零售銷售。","ok":["consumer","customer"],"best":"consumer","why":"總體經濟指標用 consumer confidence；customer confidence 指對某店的信任。"}]},
{"id":"synset-44","meaning":"公司","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"company","pos":"n.","meaning":"公司","nuance":"最通用，各種規模；work for a company","example":"Our company was founded in 1995 and now has offices in six countries.","exampleZh":"我們公司創立於 1995 年，現在在六個國家設有辦公室。"},{"word":"firm","pos":"n.","meaning":"事務所、公司","nuance":"常指小到中型專業機構，律師、會計、顧問；law firm","example":"She joined a small consulting firm after graduating.","exampleZh":"她畢業後加入一家小型顧問公司。"},{"word":"corporation","pos":"n.","meaning":"大型企業、法人","nuance":"規模大、法律上獨立的法人；multinational corporation","example":"He works for a large multinational corporation.","exampleZh":"他在一家大型跨國企業工作。"},{"word":"enterprise","pos":"n.","meaning":"企業、事業","nuance":"正式，亦指事業體或冒險事業；small enterprise / state enterprise","example":"The government supports small enterprise through low-interest loans.","exampleZh":"政府透過低利貸款支持小型企業。"},{"word":"business","pos":"n.","meaning":"商業、生意、事業","nuance":"可指企業，也指做生意本身；start a business","example":"He started his own business with only two employees.","exampleZh":"他只靠兩名員工就創辦了自己的事業。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Our ___ was founded in 1995 and now has offices in six countries.","zh":"我們公司創立於 1995 年，現在在六個國家設有辦公室。","ok":["company","corporation","enterprise","business"],"best":"company","why":"指自己公司最自然用 company；firm 較偏專業事務所。"},{"tpl":"She works for a large multinational ___.","zh":"她在一家大型跨國企業工作。","ok":["company","corporation","firm","enterprise"],"best":"corporation","why":"large multinational 搭 corporation 最道地。"},{"tpl":"He started his own ___ with only two employees.","zh":"他只靠兩名員工創辦了自己的事業。","ok":["company","firm","business","enterprise"],"best":"business","why":"創業用 start a business 是固定搭配。"}]},
{"id":"synset-45","meaning":"問題","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"problem","pos":"n.","meaning":"問題、麻煩","nuance":"最通用，指需要解決的狀況；have a problem with","example":"We need to discuss a problem with the shipment.","exampleZh":"我們需要討論貨運的一個問題。"},{"word":"issue","pos":"n.","meaning":"議題、問題","nuance":"比 problem 委婉中性，也指討論議題；raise an issue","example":"Staffing is the main issue facing the sales department.","exampleZh":"人力配置是業務部面臨的主要議題。"},{"word":"concern","pos":"n.","meaning":"疑慮、關切","nuance":"強調擔心與憂慮；raise a concern / main concern","example":"Safety is our main concern when choosing a supplier.","exampleZh":"選擇供應商時，安全是我們最大的顧慮。"},{"word":"trouble","pos":"n.","meaning":"麻煩、困擾","nuance":"口語，不可數為主；have trouble doing / in trouble","example":"I am having trouble logging into the system.","exampleZh":"我登入系統遇到困難。"},{"word":"difficulty","pos":"n.","meaning":"困難","nuance":"比 problem 強調做起來吃力；have difficulty (in) doing","example":"Several users had difficulty installing the update.","exampleZh":"幾位使用者在安裝更新時遇到困難。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"We need to discuss a ___ with the shipment.","zh":"我們需要討論貨運的一個問題。","ok":["problem","concern","difficulty"],"best":"problem","why":"具體待解決的狀況用 problem；trouble 不可數，不能加 a。"},{"tpl":"I am having ___ logging into the system.","zh":"我登入系統遇到困難。","ok":["trouble","difficulty"],"best":"trouble","why":"have trouble doing 是固定句型；difficulty 也可；problem 要用複數，單數不通。"},{"tpl":"Safety is our main ___ when choosing a supplier.","zh":"選擇供應商時，安全是我們的主要考量。","ok":["concern","issue"],"best":"concern","why":"「最在意的事」用 concern；problem 變成「安全是個麻煩」。"}]},
{"id":"synset-46","meaning":"目標","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"goal","pos":"n.","meaning":"目標","nuance":"最通用，努力想達成的結果；set / reach a goal","example":"Our main goal this year is to cut costs by 10 percent.","exampleZh":"我們今年的主要目標是削減百分之十成本。"},{"word":"objective","pos":"n.","meaning":"（具體的）目標","nuance":"正式、可衡量，常用於計畫書與會議；business objective","example":"The objective of the training is to improve customer service.","exampleZh":"這項訓練的目標是提升客戶服務。"},{"word":"target","pos":"n.","meaning":"指標、目標額度","nuance":"數字化的指標；meet / exceed a target","example":"The sales team exceeded its quarterly target.","exampleZh":"業務團隊超越了季度目標。"},{"word":"aim","pos":"n.","meaning":"目的、意圖","nuance":"偏意圖與方向，較不強調量化；the aim of","example":"The aim of the survey is to understand customer needs.","exampleZh":"這份調查的目的是了解顧客需求。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Our main ___ this year is to cut costs by 10 percent.","zh":"我們今年的主要目標是削減百分之十成本。","ok":["goal","objective","target","aim"],"best":"goal","why":"泛指想達成的結果用 goal；target 偏數字指標。"},{"tpl":"The sales team exceeded its quarterly ___.","zh":"業務團隊超越了季度目標。","ok":["target","goal","objective"],"best":"target","why":"exceed/meet a target 是固定搭配，數字化指標。"},{"tpl":"The ___ of the training is to improve customer service.","zh":"這項訓練的目的是提升客戶服務。","ok":["aim","goal","objective"],"best":"objective","why":"計畫書、課程說明常用 objective；aim 較泛，target 不合。"}]},
{"id":"synset-47","meaning":"然而","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"however","pos":"adv.","meaning":"然而","nuance":"最通用的轉折副詞；放句首或句中，前後須用逗號或分號","example":"The results were good; however, costs were higher than expected.","exampleZh":"結果不錯，然而成本比預期高。"},{"word":"nevertheless","pos":"adv.","meaning":"儘管如此","nuance":"比 however 更強調「雖然如此，仍…」，正式","example":"The plan is risky. Nevertheless, we should proceed.","exampleZh":"這個計畫有風險，儘管如此，我們仍應執行。"},{"word":"nonetheless","pos":"adv.","meaning":"儘管如此","nuance":"與 nevertheless 近乎同義，更書面","example":"The task was difficult; nonetheless, the team finished early.","exampleZh":"任務很困難，儘管如此，團隊提早完成。"},{"word":"yet","pos":"conj.","meaning":"然而、但是","nuance":"連接詞，位於兩個子句之間；語氣比 but 更強調對比","example":"The offer sounds generous, yet I have some reservations.","exampleZh":"這個提議聽起來很慷慨，然而我有些保留。"},{"word":"but","pos":"conj.","meaning":"但是","nuance":"最口語中性的轉折連接詞，不用逗號分號即可連接子句","example":"The plan is simple, but it works.","exampleZh":"計畫很簡單，但很有效。"},{"word":"still","pos":"adv.","meaning":"儘管如此、還是","nuance":"口語，句首副詞表示「即使如此」","example":"The fee is high. Still, it is worth paying.","exampleZh":"費用很高，不過還是值得付。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"The plan is risky; ___, it could double our revenue.","zh":"這個計畫有風險；然而它可能讓我們的營收翻倍。","ok":["however","nevertheless","nonetheless","still"],"best":"however","why":"分號後接逗號的轉折用 however 最自然；nevertheless/nonetheless 更正式。"},{"tpl":"The results were disappointing; ___, the team remained optimistic.","zh":"結果令人失望；儘管如此，團隊仍然樂觀。","ok":["nevertheless","nonetheless","however","still"],"best":"nevertheless","why":"「儘管如此仍…」用 nevertheless。"},{"tpl":"The offer sounds generous, ___ I have some reservations.","zh":"這個提議聽起來很慷慨，然而我有些保留。","ok":["yet","but"],"best":"yet","why":"連接詞位置用 yet；however/nevertheless 需要分號與逗號，不能原樣代入。"}]},
{"id":"synset-48","meaning":"因此","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"therefore","pos":"adv.","meaning":"因此","nuance":"最通用的結論連接詞，邏輯推論","example":"The contract expired; therefore, we can no longer use the software.","exampleZh":"合約已到期，因此我們不能再使用這套軟體。"},{"word":"thus","pos":"adv.","meaning":"因此、如此","nuance":"正式，也可表示「以此方式」","example":"The warehouse flooded, and thus all shipments were delayed.","exampleZh":"倉庫淹水，因此所有出貨都延誤了。"},{"word":"consequently","pos":"adv.","meaning":"結果、因而","nuance":"強調前因後果的連貫；偏書面","example":"Demand fell sharply; consequently, we reduced production.","exampleZh":"需求大幅下滑，因而我們減少了產量。"},{"word":"as a result","pos":"phr.","meaning":"結果","nuance":"最口語易懂，強調事件的結果","example":"The flight was canceled, and as a result we had to rebook.","exampleZh":"班機被取消，結果我們得重新訂位。"},{"word":"hence","pos":"adv.","meaning":"因此、由此","nuance":"很正式、簡短，常接名詞片語或子句","example":"The demand was low, hence the decision to cut prices.","exampleZh":"需求低迷，因此決定降價。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Demand fell sharply; ___, we reduced production.","zh":"需求大幅下滑；因此我們減少了產量。","ok":["therefore","consequently","as a result","thus","hence"],"best":"consequently","why":"分號後接逗號的因果句；thus/hence 較正式。"},{"tpl":"The flight was canceled, and ___ we had to rebook the tickets.","zh":"班機被取消，因此我們得重訂機票。","ok":["therefore","as a result","consequently","thus","hence"],"best":"as a result","why":"and 之後接結果最自然用 as a result；其他也可。"}]},
{"id":"synset-49","meaning":"此外","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"in addition","pos":"phr.","meaning":"此外","nuance":"中性正式，補充相關資訊；in addition to + N 另有用法","example":"The hotel is near the airport; in addition, it offers a free shuttle.","exampleZh":"旅館靠近機場；此外還提供免費接駁車。"},{"word":"moreover","pos":"adv.","meaning":"而且、再者","nuance":"正式、加強論點，補充更強的理由","example":"The hotel is near the airport; moreover, it offers a free shuttle.","exampleZh":"旅館靠近機場，而且還提供免費接駁車。"},{"word":"furthermore","pos":"adv.","meaning":"此外","nuance":"書面最正式，用於論述性文章與報告","example":"The system is secure; furthermore, it is easy to maintain.","exampleZh":"系統很安全；此外也容易維護。"},{"word":"besides","pos":"adv.","meaning":"再說、況且","nuance":"口語，補充一個更有力的理由","example":"I cannot join the trip; besides, I have a deadline.","exampleZh":"我不能參加旅行；再說我還有截止日。"},{"word":"also","pos":"adv.","meaning":"也、還","nuance":"最基本，補充資訊，放句中","example":"The software is easy to use and also affordable.","exampleZh":"這套軟體好用，而且價格也親民。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"The hotel is close to the airport; ___, it offers a free shuttle.","zh":"旅館靠近機場；此外還提供免費接駁車。","ok":["moreover","furthermore","in addition","besides"],"best":"moreover","why":"分號後的補充用 moreover/furthermore；besides 口語。"},{"tpl":"I cannot join the trip; I have a deadline, and ___, I do not feel well.","zh":"我不能去旅行；我有截止日，而且我也不舒服。","ok":["besides","moreover","in addition","furthermore"],"best":"besides","why":"口語說出更有力的理由用 besides。"}]},
{"id":"synset-50","meaning":"因為（介系詞片語）","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"because of","pos":"phr.","meaning":"因為","nuance":"最通用，後接名詞；口語、書面皆可","example":"The shipment was delayed because of bad weather.","exampleZh":"貨物因為壞天氣而延誤。"},{"word":"due to","pos":"phr.","meaning":"由於","nuance":"正式，後接名詞；常放在 be 動詞後或名詞後","example":"The delay was due to a mechanical fault.","exampleZh":"延誤是由於機械故障。"},{"word":"owing to","pos":"phr.","meaning":"由於","nuance":"書面、英式色彩；多放句首或句尾","example":"Owing to staff shortages, the store will close early.","exampleZh":"由於人手不足，商店會提早打烊。"},{"word":"as a result of","pos":"phr.","meaning":"由於…的結果","nuance":"強調前因造成後果，後接名詞","example":"Profits fell as a result of rising costs.","exampleZh":"由於成本上升，利潤下滑。"},{"word":"thanks to","pos":"phr.","meaning":"多虧","nuance":"正面原因，帶感激口吻","example":"Sales rose thanks to the new advertising campaign.","exampleZh":"多虧新的廣告活動，銷售上升。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"The shipment was delayed ___ bad weather.","zh":"貨物因為壞天氣而延誤。","ok":["because of","due to","owing to","as a result of"],"best":"because of","why":"原因為負面時 thanks to 不適用；because of 最通用。"},{"tpl":"Sales rose ___ the new advertising campaign.","zh":"多虧新的廣告活動，銷售上升。","ok":["thanks to","because of","due to","owing to","as a result of"],"best":"thanks to","why":"正面原因、帶感謝語氣最適合 thanks to。"},{"tpl":"The cancellation of the flight, ___ a mechanical fault, left 200 passengers stranded.","zh":"因機械故障而取消的班機讓兩百名乘客受困。","ok":["due to","owing to","because of"],"best":"due to","why":"名詞後修飾用 due to 最道地。"}]},
{"id":"synset-51","meaning":"幾乎／大約","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"almost","pos":"adv.","meaning":"幾乎（差一點）","nuance":"接近但未達；almost all / almost finished","example":"We have almost finished the audit.","exampleZh":"我們幾乎完成稽核了。"},{"word":"nearly","pos":"adv.","meaning":"幾乎、將近","nuance":"與 almost 近似；nearly 300 表示略少於 300","example":"Nearly 300 people attended the conference.","exampleZh":"將近三百人出席了研討會。"},{"word":"approximately","pos":"adv.","meaning":"大約","nuance":"正式、用於數字估計，可略多或略少","example":"The project will cost approximately ten thousand dollars.","exampleZh":"這個專案大約要花一萬美元。"},{"word":"roughly","pos":"adv.","meaning":"大概","nuance":"口語偏中性，粗略估計","example":"The trip takes roughly two hours by train.","exampleZh":"搭火車大約要兩小時。"},{"word":"about","pos":"adv.","meaning":"大約","nuance":"最口語，數字前","example":"The meeting lasted about an hour.","exampleZh":"會議持續了大約一個小時。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"The conference attracted ___ 300 participants.","zh":"研討會吸引了大約三百位參加者。","ok":["approximately","roughly","about","almost","nearly"],"best":"approximately","why":"估計人數用 approximately 最正式；almost/nearly 表示略少於 300。"},{"tpl":"We have ___ finished the audit.","zh":"我們幾乎完成了稽核。","ok":["almost","nearly"],"best":"almost","why":"表示快完成用 almost/nearly；approximately、roughly 用於數字估計。"},{"tpl":"The new model costs ___ $2,000, give or take.","zh":"新機型大約兩千美元，上下略有差距。","ok":["approximately","roughly","about"],"best":"approximately","why":"give or take 表示可能略多略少，almost/nearly 只能指略少於。"}]},
{"id":"synset-52","meaning":"最近","stars":4,"members":[{"word":"recently","pos":"adv.","meaning":"最近","nuance":"最通用，搭過去式或現在完成式","example":"We have recently updated our return policy.","exampleZh":"我們最近更新了退貨政策。"},{"word":"lately","pos":"adv.","meaning":"近來","nuance":"多用於現在完成式或進行式，句尾常見","example":"Customer complaints have increased lately.","exampleZh":"客戶抱怨近來增加了。"},{"word":"of late","pos":"phr.","meaning":"近來","nuance":"書面、略古典，同 lately","example":"Sales have been weak of late.","exampleZh":"銷售近來疲弱。"},{"word":"in recent weeks","pos":"phr.","meaning":"最近幾週","nuance":"指明一段近期時間，常用於報導","example":"Demand for electric vehicles has surged in recent weeks.","exampleZh":"電動車需求最近幾週急速攀升。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Our website has been updated ___.","zh":"我們的網站最近更新過了。","ok":["recently","lately","in recent weeks"],"best":"recently","why":"recently 最通用；lately 多用於持續性狀態，單一更新動作較不自然。"},{"tpl":"Customer complaints have increased ___.","zh":"客戶抱怨最近增加了。","ok":["lately","recently","of late","in recent weeks"],"best":"lately","why":"句尾放現在完成式，lately 最道地；of late 較書面。"}]},
{"id":"synset-53","meaning":"最後／終於","stars":4,"members":[{"word":"finally","pos":"adv.","meaning":"終於、最後","nuance":"最通用，等了很久後發生，或列舉最後項目","example":"The two firms finally signed the agreement.","exampleZh":"兩家公司終於簽署了協議。"},{"word":"eventually","pos":"adv.","meaning":"最終","nuance":"經過時間或過程之後，不一定歷經等待","example":"The project was eventually completed on time.","exampleZh":"專案最終如期完成。"},{"word":"ultimately","pos":"adv.","meaning":"歸根結柢","nuance":"強調根本層面的結論；ultimately responsible","example":"The decision ultimately rests with the board of directors.","exampleZh":"這個決定最終取決於董事會。"},{"word":"at last","pos":"phr.","meaning":"終於（如釋重負）","nuance":"表示久盼終至，帶情緒","example":"Our visas have arrived at last.","exampleZh":"我們的簽證終於到了。"},{"word":"in the end","pos":"phr.","meaning":"最後、到頭來","nuance":"回顧事情的結局","example":"In the end, the board chose the cheaper supplier.","exampleZh":"最後董事會選了較便宜的供應商。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"After months of negotiation, the two firms ___ signed the agreement.","zh":"經過數月協商，兩家公司終於簽署協議。","ok":["finally","eventually","ultimately"],"best":"finally","why":"等待後完成用 finally；ultimately 不強調時間。"},{"tpl":"The project was delayed several times, but it was completed ___.","zh":"專案多次延誤，但最終完成。","ok":["eventually","at last","in the end"],"best":"eventually","why":"強調經過延誤後的結果；at last 帶如釋重負的感覺。"},{"tpl":"After a long wait, our visas have arrived, ___.","zh":"等了很久，簽證終於到了。","ok":["at last","finally"],"best":"at last","why":"久盼終至的心情用 at last。"}]},
{"id":"synset-54","meaning":"主要地","stars":4,"members":[{"word":"mainly","pos":"adv.","meaning":"主要地","nuance":"最通用，指最大部分的原因或成分","example":"The delay was mainly caused by a shortage of parts.","exampleZh":"延誤主要是零件短缺造成的。"},{"word":"mostly","pos":"adv.","meaning":"大部分","nuance":"指多數組成，強調比例","example":"The attendees were mostly engineers.","exampleZh":"出席者大部分是工程師。"},{"word":"primarily","pos":"adv.","meaning":"首要地","nuance":"正式，指最重要的目的或原因","example":"Our revenue comes primarily from overseas sales.","exampleZh":"我們的收入主要來自海外銷售。"},{"word":"largely","pos":"adv.","meaning":"在很大程度上","nuance":"常搭 due to / based on，指程度","example":"The success was largely due to the sales team.","exampleZh":"成功很大程度要歸功於業務團隊。"},{"word":"chiefly","pos":"adv.","meaning":"最主要地","nuance":"書面，強調首要","example":"The company exports chiefly to Southeast Asia.","exampleZh":"公司出口主要銷往東南亞。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Our revenue comes ___ from overseas sales.","zh":"我們的收入主要來自海外銷售。","ok":["mainly","primarily","mostly","largely","chiefly"],"best":"primarily","why":"指最重要的來源用 primarily；mostly 偏比例。"},{"tpl":"The delay was ___ caused by a shortage of parts.","zh":"延誤主要是零件短缺造成的。","ok":["mainly","primarily","largely","chiefly","mostly"],"best":"mainly","why":"原因說明用 mainly 最自然。"},{"tpl":"The attendees were ___ engineers.","zh":"出席者大部分是工程師。","ok":["mostly","mainly","largely","chiefly","primarily"],"best":"mostly","why":"描述組成比例用 mostly。"}]},
{"id":"synset-55","meaning":"立刻","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"immediately","pos":"adv.","meaning":"立即","nuance":"最通用、正式，沒有延遲","example":"Please report any injury immediately.","exampleZh":"任何傷害請立即通報。"},{"word":"right away","pos":"phr.","meaning":"馬上","nuance":"口語，語氣友好","example":"I will send the file right away.","exampleZh":"我馬上寄出檔案。"},{"word":"at once","pos":"phr.","meaning":"立刻","nuance":"語氣較強，近命令口吻","example":"You must leave the building at once.","exampleZh":"你們必須立刻離開大樓。"},{"word":"promptly","pos":"adv.","meaning":"迅速、準時","nuance":"強調不拖延、守時；pay promptly","example":"The invoice must be paid promptly upon receipt.","exampleZh":"發票收到後必須迅速支付。"},{"word":"instantly","pos":"adv.","meaning":"瞬間","nuance":"幾乎沒有時間差","example":"The tickets sold out instantly.","exampleZh":"票瞬間就賣光了。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"If you notice a gas leak, call the emergency number ___.","zh":"若發現瓦斯外洩，請立即撥打緊急電話。","ok":["immediately","right away","at once","promptly"],"best":"immediately","why":"緊急指示用 immediately 最清楚。"},{"tpl":"The invoice must be paid ___ upon receipt.","zh":"發票收到後必須迅速支付。","ok":["immediately","promptly"],"best":"promptly","why":"與 upon receipt 搭配的付款要求常用 promptly。"},{"tpl":"The tickets sold out ___.","zh":"票瞬間賣光。","ok":["instantly","immediately","right away","at once"],"best":"instantly","why":"強調幾乎沒有時間差用 instantly。"}]},
{"id":"synset-56","meaning":"目前","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"currently","pos":"adv.","meaning":"目前","nuance":"最通用，指現狀","example":"We are currently reviewing the applications.","exampleZh":"我們目前正在審查申請資料。"},{"word":"at present","pos":"phr.","meaning":"目前","nuance":"正式、書面","example":"Mr. Lee is out of the office at present.","exampleZh":"李先生目前不在辦公室。"},{"word":"now","pos":"adv.","meaning":"現在","nuance":"最口語基本","example":"The store is now open on Sundays.","exampleZh":"這家店現在週日也營業。"},{"word":"presently","pos":"adv.","meaning":"目前（美式）；不久（英式）","nuance":"美式指目前，英式常指不久，容易混淆；多益偏美式","example":"The company is presently negotiating a merger.","exampleZh":"公司目前正在洽談合併。"},{"word":"these days","pos":"phr.","meaning":"近來、現今","nuance":"描述習慣或趨勢","example":"Most people book flights online these days.","exampleZh":"現在多數人都在網路上訂機票。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"We are ___ reviewing the applications.","zh":"我們目前正在審查申請資料。","ok":["currently","now","presently"],"best":"currently","why":"進行式搭 currently 最典型。"},{"tpl":"Mr. Lee is out of the office ___.","zh":"李先生目前不在辦公室。","ok":["at present","currently","now"],"best":"at present","why":"句尾放 at present 最正式自然。"},{"tpl":"Most people book flights online ___.","zh":"現在多數人都在網路上訂機票。","ok":["these days","now"],"best":"these days","why":"描述普遍習慣用 these days。"}]},
{"id":"synset-57","meaning":"也許","stars":4,"members":[{"word":"perhaps","pos":"adv.","meaning":"也許","nuance":"書面、略正式","example":"We could perhaps reduce the price if the client orders more.","exampleZh":"如果客戶訂更多，我們或許可以降價。"},{"word":"maybe","pos":"adv.","meaning":"也許","nuance":"口語，最常見","example":"We could maybe reduce the price if the client orders more.","exampleZh":"如果客戶訂更多，我們也許可以降價。"},{"word":"possibly","pos":"adv.","meaning":"可能","nuance":"強調有可能，不確定","example":"The shipment will possibly arrive on Friday.","exampleZh":"貨物可能週五到。"},{"word":"probably","pos":"adv.","meaning":"很可能","nuance":"把握大於 possibly","example":"The shipment will probably arrive on Friday.","exampleZh":"貨物很可能週五到。"},{"word":"conceivably","pos":"adv.","meaning":"可想見地","nuance":"正式，指理論上有可能","example":"The merger could conceivably double our market share.","exampleZh":"這項合併理論上可能讓我們的市佔翻倍。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"We could ___ reduce the price if the client orders more.","zh":"如果客戶訂更多，我們或許可以降價。","ok":["perhaps","maybe","possibly","probably"],"best":"perhaps","why":"提出可能性的建議用 perhaps；probably 把握較高。"},{"tpl":"The shipment will ___ arrive on Friday, but I will confirm tomorrow.","zh":"貨物可能週五到，但我明天會確認。","ok":["probably","possibly","perhaps"],"best":"probably","why":"表示把握較大但待確認用 probably。"},{"tpl":"It is ___ the best offer we have received this year.","zh":"這可能是我們今年收到最好的報價。","ok":["probably","possibly","perhaps"],"best":"probably","why":"形容最佳選項時 probably 最順。"}]},
{"id":"synset-58","meaning":"可用的／可取得的","stars":4,"members":[{"word":"available","pos":"adj.","meaning":"可用的、有空的","nuance":"最通用：人有空、物品有庫存、服務可使用","example":"Is a technician available to help with the installation?","exampleZh":"有技術人員可以協助安裝嗎？"},{"word":"accessible","pos":"adj.","meaning":"可取得的、容易進入的","nuance":"強調能夠接近或使用；also 無障礙","example":"The data is accessible to all registered users.","exampleZh":"所有註冊使用者都能存取這些資料。"},{"word":"on hand","pos":"phr.","meaning":"在手邊的、備用的","nuance":"口語，就在身邊隨時可用","example":"Keep the manual on hand in case of emergency.","exampleZh":"手冊請放在手邊以備不時之需。"},{"word":"obtainable","pos":"adj.","meaning":"可取得的","nuance":"正式，指能夠買到或取得","example":"Spare parts are no longer obtainable for this older model.","exampleZh":"這款舊機型已買不到備用零件。"},{"word":"usable","pos":"adj.","meaning":"可使用的","nuance":"強調功能上能用","example":"The old servers are still usable.","exampleZh":"舊伺服器還能用。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"Is a technician ___ to help with the installation?","zh":"有技術人員可以協助安裝嗎？","ok":["available","on hand"],"best":"available","why":"詢問人員有沒有空用 available。"},{"tpl":"Please keep the manual ___ in case of emergency.","zh":"請把手冊放在手邊以備緊急之需。","ok":["on hand","available","accessible"],"best":"on hand","why":"keep sth on hand 是固定說法。"},{"tpl":"Spare parts are no longer ___ for this older model.","zh":"這款舊機型已經沒有備用零件。","ok":["available","obtainable"],"best":"available","why":"缺貨情境最常說 not available；obtainable 較正式。"}]},
{"id":"synset-59","meaning":"有效的","stars":5,"members":[{"word":"effective","pos":"adj.","meaning":"有效的、產生預期成果的","nuance":"重結果；effective way / measure","example":"The new training program proved highly effective.","exampleZh":"新的訓練課程證明非常有效。"},{"word":"efficient","pos":"adj.","meaning":"有效率的","nuance":"重投入產出比，省時省力；efficient process","example":"A more efficient process would save us hours each week.","exampleZh":"更有效率的流程每週能替我們省下數小時。"},{"word":"productive","pos":"adj.","meaning":"有生產力的","nuance":"產出多；productive meeting","example":"It was a very productive meeting.","exampleZh":"這是場非常有成效的會議。"},{"word":"workable","pos":"adj.","meaning":"可行的","nuance":"方案實際上行得通","example":"The team proposed a workable plan for the move.","exampleZh":"團隊提出了可行的搬遷計畫。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"The new training program proved highly ___.","zh":"新的訓練課程證明非常有效。","ok":["effective","productive","workable"],"best":"effective","why":"重「產生成果」用 effective；efficient 是省資源。"},{"tpl":"A more ___ process would save us hours each week.","zh":"更有效率的流程每週能替我們省下數小時。","ok":["efficient","effective","productive","workable"],"best":"efficient","why":"省時省力用 efficient。"},{"tpl":"It was a very ___ meeting; we settled all the open issues.","zh":"這是場非常有成效的會議，我們解決了所有待辦議題。","ok":["productive","effective","efficient"],"best":"productive","why":"會議產出多用 productive。"}]},
{"id":"synset-60","meaning":"方便的","stars":4,"members":[{"word":"convenient","pos":"adj.","meaning":"方便的","nuance":"最通用：時間、地點、設備方便；convenient location","example":"The hotel is in a convenient location, close to the station.","exampleZh":"旅館位置方便，靠近車站。"},{"word":"handy","pos":"adj.","meaning":"好用的、手邊方便的","nuance":"口語，小工具或技能；come in handy","example":"A pocket calculator is handy for quick estimates.","exampleZh":"口袋計算機拿來快速估算很方便。"},{"word":"accessible","pos":"adj.","meaning":"容易到達／使用的","nuance":"指易於接近，也指無障礙","example":"The new office is accessible by train and bus.","exampleZh":"新辦公室搭火車與公車都能到。"},{"word":"user-friendly","pos":"adj.","meaning":"好上手的","nuance":"產品、介面易操作","example":"The updated app is much more user-friendly for beginners.","exampleZh":"更新後的應用程式對新手好上手許多。"}],"frames":[{"tpl":"The hotel is in a ___ location, close to the station.","zh":"旅館位置方便，靠近車站。","ok":["convenient","handy"],"best":"convenient","why":"地點的便利用 convenient 最自然。"},{"tpl":"A pocket calculator is ___ for quick estimates.","zh":"口袋計算機拿來快速估算很方便。","ok":["handy","convenient"],"best":"handy","why":"小工具好用用 handy。"},{"tpl":"The updated app is much more ___ for first-time users.","zh":"更新後的應用程式對首次使用者好上手許多。","ok":["user-friendly","convenient","accessible"],"best":"user-friendly","why":"介面易操作用 user-friendly。"}]}
